{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar","id":782270,"title":"What is a Lunar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-08T06:57:39-08:00","id":782270,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What is a Lunar?","content":"What is a Lunar? I know they are not simply Shapeshifters or Animorphs. They often get Pigeon-holed into &quot;Savage Barbarian Warrior&quot;, but that is a very two dimensional view of the splat. Lunars are not Garou, Warriors/Protectors of Gaia. <br /> <br /> So what are they? Are the the Premier Predators of Creation? A malleable Jack of All Trades, in contrast to a Solar's Supernal master of one? The Exalted Equivalent of a Swiss Army Knife?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:06:52-08:00","id":782273,"title":"","content":"as far as i know, after 2 entire editions of exalted, we have been promised the answer to your question when the 3e lunars book drops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:08:04-08:00","id":782275,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Monsters with virtue to them, or the virtuous with monstrous inner features.</a> Have you read through Cult of the Illuminated? The Lunar companion Faithful Pia is a fairly good illustration of this. She's noted as being desperate to be harmless, but can turn into what is at least textually, if not mechanically, described as a tail-lashing monster that can tear things apart, should someone push her too far. While her original 1e description was a bit too much of a curse-type werewolf story (not a Werewolf story in caps indicating W:tA), you don't have to remove or change many things to fit the essence of what it seems that the developers were going for as a concept for Lunars into EX3. She has a strong duality that makes her seem completely innocent yet has seen some shit and can fall into pure viciousness. Anything about attempted abduction by the Silver Pact or chimerae can fall to the wayside, if you get your hands on CotI and check it out.<br /> <br /> So, basically, a unity of conflicting opposites at the most extreme ends, combined with some aspects of various werebeast legends because Luna loves Gaia and her Exalted are explicitly shaped by this affection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:10:45-08:00","id":782279,"title":"","content":"I think one could get something out of the idea of &quot;savage barbarian warrior&quot; being an aesthetic and a structure to their powers without really informing who they are as people.<br /> <br /> I've a basic idea of a combination of latent savagery, some iconic feats for each Attribute, and invoking and referencing legendary beast powers. I'm pretty sure I've had an idea about versatility beyond &quot;an Attribute Excellency let's you add a lot of power to an Ability without being very good at it&quot;, but I can't quite remember what it was.<br /> <br /> But between that and the utility of shapeshifting, that's mostly versatility as an emergent thing rather than their big focus, which is something I think doesn't work very well and should be dropped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:11:14-08:00","id":782280,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaphod_Beeblebrox\" target=\"_blank\">Lunars are just these guys, you know?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T08:51:31-08:00","id":782325,"title":"","content":"I rather suspect that this question is its own answer. That is to say, each Lunar will have his or her or his/her or whatever other pronoun you want to use own answer to it, because collectively, they're not entirely certain <i>who</i> they are anymore.<br /> <br /> Once they were the Solars' boon companions, their spouses, partners, confidants, and lieutenants, but then the Solars died and the Lunars... changed, and kept on changing. I imagine there are a great many Lunars who do not wish to go back to being what they once were, because each is determined and <i>able</i> to decide what they are now, themselves.<br /> <br /> From what I've read of the devs' comments on Lunars, that's at least one aspect of their identities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:17:28-08:00","id":782367,"title":"","content":"Lunars are people who broke their chains.<br /> <br /> Luna looked down upon the world and saw heroes after her own heart; people willing to face the consequences of running away from their enslavers, their stifling homes, their controlling parents, their oppressive religions, their financial debts, their sworn oaths. These people were brave enough to run after freedom, even if it killed them.<br /> <br /> One of the Lunars in the corebook was being shipped back to the Realm to serve as a sex slave. She threw herself into shark-infested waters to be eaten alive or drowned to death. Luna decided that such courage should be Exalted.<br /> <br /> To these brave souls, Luna grants the freedom of shapeshifting. No longer are you confined to the form in which you are born. With your Tell as your kite string, you soar around the full spectrum of human appearance with your true form. With your totem, you can automatically assume the form of the animal that most reflects you, and even assume a were-beast form of incredible power. Heart's Blood allows you to take any animal form you want as well.<br /> <br /> She also offers the freedom of raw power and versatility, because Lunar Exalted are second only to Solars and their ilk in that regard. The Sidereals and Alchemicals don't come close, because of the restrictions on each of their Charmsets.<br /> <br /> The primary Lunar narrative is ALSO about freedom, because they're faced with the Realm and Sidereals who want to deny them the freedom to LIVE, and the return of the Solars threatens the Lunar freedom to choose to become something different than they were in the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:06:15-08:00","id":782423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar#post782270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>A miserable little pile of secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:04:28-08:00","id":782482,"title":"","content":"We've spent a lot of time trying to answer this question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:18:57-08:00","id":782492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782482#post782482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've spent a lot of time trying to answer this question.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the vein of this pursuit, and spirit of our actual, real-world moon looking different from night to night but actually remaining constant because of perspective and lighting, I want an Ex3 Appearance Charm that works like Dreams and Expectations Stance/River Reflects Desire by evoking the parable of the five blind men and the elephant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T18:57:27-08:00","id":782578,"title":"","content":"There are a few major ways to look at Lunars.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Military Outlook:</b></u><br /> Consider that all the Exalt types were designed to fight in the Primordial War. Thus each type had to have some sort of function, a role to play or a job to do. Lunars are the ultimate spec-ops exalt type. They infiltrate enemy territory, they cause massive supply disruptions and they can turn produce their own armies out of the locals (or local wild life). This is further supported by the fact that out of all the exalt types, Lunars gain the least benefit from artifacts. Why purchase an artifact skyship when you can fly on your own, why get a daiklave when you can create claws, etc. This means that they are self contained and not dependent on supply lines or access to friendly military support.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Easy Story Outlook: </b></u><br /> A different method to look at Lunars is from a Storytelling perspective. Nothing is expected of them in the greater narrative of the Exalted setting. A solar is expected to reshape the world, an Abyssal is expected to end it, an Infernal is expected to unleash hell on Creation, the Sidereals are expected to maintain the status quo, and the Terrestrials are supposed to breed and make bad decisions.<br /> <br /> But a Lunar can just be a barbarian, they can be a scholar, they can be anything. The amount of animalism or barbarism in any given Lunar is completely up to the player. It makes just as much sense for a Lunar to build a City State as it does to be a murder-hobo. Thus Lunars are the Exalt type for Players who don't want any of the other exalt types preconceived notions and for the STs that want to run a Celestial Exalt game without the Celestial Exalt expectations. I mean you can run a Lunar game with all the characters being in Realm Secondary school complete with anime high school tropes and it wouldn't feel that out of place.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Business Model:</u></b><br /> Consider that Furrys, transhumanism, Totems and other related themes tend to sell well to certain aspects of nerd culture. The Lunars are there to check a box so that the animal focused players have something to default to when looking at Exalted as a game system to invest in. Speaking of niche appeal, this also applies to Alchemicals. Funny how both niche types are so similar in mechanics design and concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":727,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","user":"Thoth","date":". 12-08-2015, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T19:05:58-08:00","id":782580,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782578#post782578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few major ways to look at Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782578#post782578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b><u>The Military Outlook:</u></b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Was leaving this post empty a form of sarcasm, metacommentary, or just hitting 'post reply' by accident? :P</span></span><br /> <br /> Edit: And now he's edited his post and I look like a doof.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u200b</span> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782423#post782423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">A miserable little pile of secrets.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Enough talk! Have at you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","user":"Korhal_IV","date":". 12-08-2015, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T19:11:01-08:00","id":782581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782423#post782423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A miserable little pile of secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I was soooooooo tempted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T21:05:20-08:00","id":782605,"title":"","content":"All I know is that if they keep the heartsblood mechanics from 2e then there's no power on this earth that will separate Lunars from &quot;crazed barbarian savage&quot; themes. It's really hard to sell the idea of a civilized Lunar who periodically rips out animal hearts and eats them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T21:36:29-08:00","id":782614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782578#post782578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few major ways to look at Lunars.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Military Outlook:</b></u><br /> Consider that all the Exalt types were designed to fight in the Primordial War. Thus each type had to have some sort of function, a role to play or a job to do. Lunars are the ultimate spec-ops exalt type. They infiltrate enemy territory, they cause massive supply disruptions and they can turn produce their own armies out of the locals (or local wild life). This is further supported by the fact that out of all the exalt types, Lunars gain the least benefit from artifacts. Why purchase an artifact skyship when you can fly on your own, why get a daiklave when you can create claws, etc. This means that they are self contained and not dependent on supply lines or access to friendly military support.</div> </div> </div> </div>This had issues even in 2nd edition, which was super-hellbent on structuring the Exalted in a certain way in character and out. By the time Glories hit, we learned that the Incarnae couldn't actually design their Exalted to do anything other than be humans with powers patterned after the patron deity in question; this retconned out the &quot;Unconquered Sun forced Luna to make Lunars subservient to Solars&quot; detail as well. Also, in EX3, what Lunars are now is different than what they were in the Old Realm's span of rule or the Primordial War; whatever you see of them now doesn't hold true for any point you might want to make about past ages. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>The Easy Story Outlook: </b></u><br /> A different method to look at Lunars is from a Storytelling perspective. Nothing is expected of them in the greater narrative of the Exalted setting. A solar is expected to reshape the world, an Abyssal is expected to end it, an Infernal is expected to unleash hell on Creation, the Sidereals are expected to maintain the status quo, and the Terrestrials are supposed to breed and make bad decisions.<br /> <br /> But a Lunar can just be a barbarian, they can be a scholar, they can be anything. The amount of animalism or barbarism in any given Lunar is completely up to the player. It makes just as much sense for a Lunar to build a City State as it does to be a murder-hobo. Thus Lunars are the Exalt type for Players who don't want any of the other exalt types preconceived notions and for the STs that want to run a Celestial Exalt game without the Celestial Exalt expectations. I mean you can run a Lunar game with all the characters being in Realm Secondary school complete with anime high school tropes and it wouldn't feel that out of place.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Business Model:</u></b><br /> Consider that Furrys, transhumanism, Totems and other related themes tend to sell well to certain aspects of nerd culture. The Lunars are there to check a box so that the animal focused players have something to default to when looking at Exalted as a game system to invest in. Speaking of niche appeal, this also applies to Alchemicals. Funny how both niche types are so similar in mechanics design and concept. </div> </div> </div>Furry fandom is something quite a bit different from shapeshifting beast-themed Exalted. It's an old saw that most people who identify with furries and who do play Exalted tend to just make Solar beastfolk, because most of those characters don't really get the same thing out of their appearance that the shapeshifting Lunars would (the fact that Lunars will often not spend time in their alleged &quot;furry&quot; form and tend to use that form explicitly to be a murder machine probably puts a lot of prospective anthropomorphic fans off of choosing them; rather than just being a lion or wolf person, the Lunar is the beast as a raging apocalyptic war avatar, a decidedly loaded feature). Also, it's really easy; you can make Solar beastfolk using just a few merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T21:44:25-08:00","id":782616,"title":"","content":"See, Solars are humans who have been exalted with the essence of the Unconquered Sun, giving them supreme excellence and a theme of rulership and sunshine.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Lunars are humans who have been exalted with the essence of Luna, giving them ... who is...<br /> ... hmmm,<i> I see the problem.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T22:07:40-08:00","id":782627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782605#post782605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that if they keep the heartsblood mechanics from 2e then there's no power on this earth that will separate Lunars from &quot;crazed barbarian savage&quot; themes. It's really hard to sell the idea of a civilized Lunar who periodically rips out animal hearts and eats them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said it before, I'll say it again: <b>No heart-ripping or -eating is necessary. Even in 2e, all you have to do is kill it and taste its blood.</b> You don't even have to hunt it yourself. There's been thread after thread after thread about this, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T22:12:41-08:00","id":782628,"title":"","content":"Lunars are Lunars.<br /> <br /> This is kind of a cheap answer, but it's also true and important because there is a strange tendency to try to answer this kind of question by looking at things that aren't Lunars, but carry a facet that Lunars also share, and say &quot;this facet is Lunars&quot;. In truth, Lunars have all those facets, but are none of them in entirety.<br /> <br /> As for what those facets are, well, problem is, at least for the 3rd Edition, we don't have the book yet. This might also seem like a cheap answer, but it's also true, especially given how heavily some Exalt types were changed from their previous edition counterparts (such as Abyssals going from eternally hunted bad decision makers, a story that I adored, to romantic inscrutable emos, a story that I have no idea how to work with until the actual Abyssals book comes out and I see a full picture). You can, of course, try to give your own interpretations based on the limited information we have, but that nearly always leads to disappointment when the final product isn't exactly how you interpreted it would be.<br /> <br /> ((Also, Lunars don't rip out hearts and eat them in 2nd Edition. They hunt an animal (or other entity), kill it, and drink its heart's blood. Given that our &quot;civilized society&quot; regularly does far worse without as much tangible benefit, the distinction should be non-trivial to many.))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T22:24:56-08:00","id":782631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782614#post782614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This had issues even in 2nd edition, which was super-hellbent on structuring the Exalted in a certain way in character and out. By the time Glories hit, we learned that the Incarnae couldn't actually design their Exalted to do anything other than be humans with powers patterned after the patron deity in question; this retconned out the &quot;Unconquered Sun forced Luna to make Lunars subservient to Solars&quot; detail as well. Also, in EX3, what Lunars are now is different than what they were in the Old Realm's span of rule or the Primordial War; whatever you see of them now doesn't hold true for any point you might want to make about past ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>During development of first edition the Lunars were corrupted Exalted of the Wyld, think Fair Folk exalts. Once First Edition came out the Lunars were the precursors to the Garou and other changing breeds in the W:tA setting. Second Edition comes around and they have completely ret conned the cWoD connection and made Exalted a stand alone line.<br /> <br /> First Edition Luna was the companion of the Unconquered Sun, then Luna became a matahari that seduced Gaia. Second Edition then comes out with concept that really Luna and Gaia were the real pairing and the Sun &amp; Moon combo is almost just for show. The list goes on and on and on. Everything about Lunars has been retconned so many times that in truth none of it makes sense. The Luna is vague and used as filler, the Lunar exalts themselves lack design focus and more importantly agency. It wouldn't be so bad if they actually did stuff during the entire absence of the Solars, but at best they were given a backfilled explanation that some how a few hundred Lunars held back the entirety of the Wyld forces after the Contagion.<br /> <br /> You will note that I gave methods of looking at the Lunars, not canon answers of how they should be used. As for Ex.3, until it has actually come out, been published, finalized and White Wolf is working on the expansions, there is no reason to bear it any mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782614#post782614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furry fandom is something quite a bit different from shapeshifting beast-themed Exalted. It's an old saw that most people who identify with furries and who do play Exalted tend to just make Solar beastfolk, because most of those characters don't really get the same thing out of their appearance that the shapeshifting Lunars would (the fact that Lunars will often not spend time in their alleged &quot;furry&quot; form and tend to use that form explicitly to be a murder machine probably puts a lot of prospective anthropomorphic fans off of choosing them; rather than just being a lion or wolf person, the Lunar is the beast as a raging apocalyptic war avatar, a decidedly loaded feature). Also, it's really easy; you can make Solar beastfolk using just a few merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>But with a few merits you can do the same with any exalt type. As I pointed out, Lunars don't have to be anything. Thus on a mechanical and storyline level they work well for people who are in the game for the aesthetics rather than the power gaming, body count or empire building.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T22:57:29-08:00","id":782638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782605#post782605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that if they keep the heartsblood mechanics from 2e then there's no power on this earth that will separate Lunars from &quot;crazed barbarian savage&quot; themes. It's really hard to sell the idea of a civilized Lunar who periodically rips out animal hearts and eats them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that that isn't too rare for modern hunters to do (granted, they use knives and so on to cut out the heart and usually cook it) I wouldn't say that's a &quot;crazed barbarian savage&quot; thing exclusively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T23:04:06-08:00","id":782640,"title":"","content":"And if in third edition the book actually <i>talks</i> about these perfectly civilized ways of preparing heartsblood, then there will finally be room to grow out of barbarism as a theme. Second edition could NOT let this mental image die, however, and so far I don't see anything that makes me expect we'll have better luck with the new book.<br /> <br /> That said, at least the new Lunars are heavily motivated and they have their own antagonists in the sidereals and immaculate faith. They were always being hunted but now they writers have them actually <i>doing</i> something about it en mass, which is an improvement. Whether that paints them into a corner as &quot;anti-establishment&quot; we shall have to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-09-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T23:24:17-08:00","id":782647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782628#post782628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">((Also, Lunars don't rip out hearts and eat them in 2nd Edition. They hunt an animal (or other entity), kill it, and drink its heart's blood. Given that our &quot;civilized society&quot; regularly does far worse without as much tangible benefit, the distinction should be non-trivial to many.))</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the &quot;heart's blood&quot; term at fault. Somehow people keep focusing on this <i>ill defined</i> climax of the ritual and neglecting the whole &quot;sacred hunt&quot; aspect of shapestealing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782627#post782627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before, I'll say it again: <b>No heart-ripping or -eating is necessary. Even in 2e, all you have to do is kill it and taste its blood.</b> You don't even have to hunt it yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor correction: You don't have to hunt it <b>by</b> yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T23:55:57-08:00","id":782656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782647#post782647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor correction: You don't have to hunt it <b>by</b> yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that the animal can be placed before you, bound in chains and unable to move or fight back, such that you killing it is more of a slaughter than a personal hunt, YES, you can take its Heart's Blood without personally hunting it.<br /> <br /> It's enough that you had the resolve to kill it and take its blood. YOU killed it. YOU consumed it. It's yours.<br /> <br /> HOW you got to the point of being able to kill it is irrelevant; the method doesn't matter. You can hunt with automatic rifles from helicopters, you can leave out poisoned food, you can PAY people to hunt it down for you.<br /> <br /> In 2.5 Glories, one of the Othermoons LET Luna kill and eat her as a voluntary sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T01:31:47-08:00","id":782688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782423#post782423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A miserable little pile of secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went into this topic wanting to say that. Curse you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T02:43:14-08:00","id":782703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really hard to sell the idea of a civilized Lunar who periodically rips out animal hearts and eats them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only to people with fairly biased definitions of &quot;civilized&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T08:16:18-08:00","id":782811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782581#post782581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I was soooooooo tempted.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782688#post782688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went into this topic wanting to say that. Curse you!</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't believe I was the first person to say it; especially since it's actually pretty true in this case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:26:01-08:00","id":782855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782616#post782616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, Solars are humans who have been exalted with the essence of the Unconquered Sun, giving them supreme excellence and a theme of rulership and sunshine.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Lunars are humans who have been exalted with the essence of Luna, giving them ... who is...<br /> ... hmmm,<i> I see the problem.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this might be overstating the problem (if I'm understanding the post correctly). From what I understand, you're confused as to what Luna might be with regards to her Chosen, such that they might become Lunar? If that's the case, I can say that it's not that difficult to do. Here's something I have thought up recently (actually whilst looking at the moon outside at night).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the full moon, Luna reveals her full glory, beautiful and terrible. Her power is obvious, and inspires worship, desire, and terror. She shines brilliantly upon Creation, an implicit threat to all those who would defy her. At the full moon, Luna\u2019s power is explicit, and her might shines to all those who would dare to witness it, overpowering all others in the night sky. Full Moon Lunars are empowered by Luna in this state, and oftentimes their power is equally clear, albeit on a mortal scale. They are the fiercest warriors, the swiftest hunters, and can survive far more than any living body should.<br /> <br /> During the new moon, Luna\u2019s power is hidden by her mystery. Though she does not seem to be there, her presence is implicit in the night sky. The wise fear these nights more than those during which she reveals her fullest glory, for although she cannot be seen, Luna remains vigilant. Luna in this state is unknown to all but her Chosen, and her mysteries are just as powerful as her glory. No Moon Lunars are granted the power to emulate Luna in this state. Unlike the Twilights of the Solars, No Moons are not revealers of great truths, though they may discover them, nor are they builders of great things, though some may construct things. Rather, No Moons are discoverers of mysteries, unlocking secrets and using them as they see fit. Their power may be subtler than their fellow Lunars, but it is just as real.<br /> <br /> In those times between full and new moons, Luna hides her full glory, but remains visible, a gorgeous figure dancing through the night sky. In these states, Luna\u2019s terror is hidden, leaving only her beauty readily apparent, but the terror persists nonetheless, and those who find her beauty will find both. The changing moon reveals only that which Luna wishes, while the rest remains hidden, and what is revealed may mislead those who believe it is the entire truth of her being. The Changing Moons reflect this aspect of Luna. Beautiful, enticing, and/or magnetic, they are often the center of attention wherever they go, and use this to their advantage. Changing Moons reveal what parts of themselves they wish, drawing in those who might have use to them, only for their hidden sides emerge when the time is right... </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously, this might not be what the devs do with it, but it shows that Luna can be shown to have concrete themes, even though one of them is change. Also, I'm aware that there's a great deal of flexibility between the castes, perhaps even greater than among Solars (by simple virtue of attribute charms), but I think that cores such as these might be acceptable concepts for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T12:16:34-08:00","id":782987,"title":"","content":"These threads never sum an Exalt, but! still, my reflections at the moment:<br /> <br /> The Lunars: Mighty heroes of humanity who achieve great deeds of legend for man by reshaping their bodies and minds, to take on the strengths of animals and monsters.<br /> <br /> As for the Chosen of Luna, and what that means, thinking about it for a second, I'm interested in Luna as an outsider hero among the pantheon of the Incarna.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is the king, which means that, like a king, he expects of obedience, service and domination of his people and in return, his compact is that he acts as a champion and vessel of their spirit. The Maidens are guides, advisors and shapers - they offer only advice, to be taken or left, guidance which can uplift, but to refuse it can come with consequences, and to take it can be to be shaped in secret. Luna's an outsider. She comes as a stranger to the pantheon, to be within it through her role as lover (to Gaea). That's not an essence you can always trust - at times it can be predatory, alienated, self interested - but it does not seek to make itself your master or your shaper (either of those chains, of sorts) and exalt itself into that role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T13:37:52-08:00","id":784959,"title":"","content":"Thou call'dst me 'dog' before thou hadst a cause;<br /> But, since I am a dog, beware my fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:33:25-08:00","id":788852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782423#post782423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A miserable little pile of shapes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T11:01:05-08:00","id":788865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782631#post782631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During development of first edition the Lunars were corruptd Exalted of the Wyld, think Fair Folk exalts. Once First Edition came out the Lunars were the precursors to the Garou and other changing breeds in the W:tA setting. Second Edition comes around and they have completely ret conned the cWoD connection and made Exalted a stand alone line.<br /> <br /> First Edition Luna was the companion of the Unconquered Sun, then Luna became a matahari that seduced Gaia. Second Edition then comes out with concept that really Luna and Gaia were the real pairing and the Sun &amp; Moon combo is almost just for show. The list goes on and on and on. Everything about Lunars has been retconned so many times that in truth none of it makes sense. The Luna is vague and used as filler, the Lunar exalts themselves lack design focus and more importantly agency. It wouldn't be so bad if they actually did stuff during the entire absence of the Solars, but at best they were given a backfilled explanation that some how a few hundred Lunars held back the entirety of the Wyld forces after the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sums it up really. They started off without a strong place in the setting and just haven't had a satisfying theme for two editions. And because of that, the fandom versions have grown in a thousand incompatible directions, and the arguments get so vituperative because there's no generally agreed core to cleave to or deviate from. 3e just needs to pick one thing (I think it barely matters what at this point), sell it well, and leave room for variations. It seems to be going in the right direction so far, at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T12:46:57-08:00","id":788925,"title":"","content":"Sadly that is what they tried to do with the Thousand Rivers society building fluff, but botched the landing.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue with Lunars is that they are Celestial level exalts that can't be allowed to be productive. Consider that if they can change the course of history like any Celestial can, then Creation would not be needing the Solars to return to &quot;fix things&quot;. If the Lunars can't make setting changes, then why are they Celestial grade exalts.<br /> <br /> I have found how badly this concept has hampered Lunars when I ran a game for some new players. They were new to RPGs and they were cutting their teeth on Exalted rather than something easier on a mechanics level. So I decided to simplify things by setting the game a few centuries prior to the Jade prison break. That way all they had to deal with was setting information, dragon-blooded and the occasional Wyld related issue. For the new players this format worked pretty well.<br /> <br /> The setting how ever started to unravel within 3 games due to smart players. The only thing that could keep the Lunars in check were sidereals and you can't roll those out every time. By the time the Jade prison broke, the Empire was in a shambles due to Lunar Predation. Things were almost to the level of cWoD where you have Vampires afraid to leave the city because the Werewolves rule the country side, except in this case the Terrestrials were afraid to leave major cities due to the Lunars and their allies. Interestingly enough this fit with the Lunar mentality of making humanity tougher through harsher treatment, but it still put the setting through a shredding machine.<br /> <br /> Fun times over all in my opinion, but in general too many STs are uncomfortable with PCs actually making changes to the setting that would alter things too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T13:19:07-08:00","id":788938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=782423#post782423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A miserable little pile of secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came to this thread just to make this joke. You beat me to it. Good job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T17:47:26-08:00","id":789044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=788852#post788852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fixed that for you!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not how chimerae work anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T18:35:31-08:00","id":789058,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a big piece of this puzzle might come from looking on the Lunar Castes as something that <i>they</i> made rather than Luna; that they don't represent functions granted by Luna in which she disseminates qualities of herself, so much as their takes on how to focus into roles within their station, that are dedicated to her. The magic that allows them to fix the No Moon Caste might be based on the iconography of the mysterious Luna, but it's ultimately more revelatory of the Exalt than the Incarna and, more importantly, is based in their actions in the Second Age. You are a Lunar who was incribed with the No Moon Caste; Chosen to be a boundless beastling because you broke your chains, and then given your Caste because your response to the hostility of a world that does not forgive unchained monsters was to survive by wit and knowledge and observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T03:49:37-08:00","id":789188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789058#post789058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if a big piece of this puzzle might come from looking on the Lunar Castes as something that <i>they</i> made rather than Luna; that they don't represent functions granted by Luna in which she disseminates qualities of herself, so much as their takes on how to focus into roles within their station, that are dedicated to her. The magic that allows them to fix the No Moon Caste might be based on the iconography of the mysterious Luna, but it's ultimately more revelatory of the Exalt than the Incarna and, more importantly, is based in their actions in the Second Age. You are a Lunar who was incribed with the No Moon Caste; Chosen to be a boundless beastling because you broke your chains, and then given your Caste because your response to the hostility of a world that does not forgive unchained monsters was to survive by wit and knowledge and observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I am misunderstanding what you are getting at, but isn't that trying to solve faulty foundation problem by creating a convoluted meta story? I mean you are already choosing the characteristics at character generation, it doesn't change anything to say that you chose that path or Luna chose you because you already embody her traits prior to exaltation.<br /> <br /> In either case you play the way you want play and the overall setting interaction and fluff is still a mess. Sadly any attempt to give narrative focus to Luna or her Exalted will inevitably cause the perception of the loss of fluidity and adaptability, which goes against the whole shape shifting, adaptable, many faced schtick. On the other hand it can be argued that because since Lunars and Luna lack a defined set of core concepts, they double as all purpose plot hole filler as the setting or game needs them.<br /> <br /> Why did Gaia defect to the gods side? Luna in tight moonsilver pants.<br /> <br /> Why didn't the Fair Folk over run Creation since they technically can be infinite in number before the Empress got inside the imperial manse? Because Lunars were doing stuff.<br /> <br /> Why aren't the remaining first age centers of power used by the Terrestrials to enhance their empires? Lunars set up shop as mini-bosses for the PCs to deal with.<br /> <br /> I dare say that Lunars are Exalteds version of History Channels &quot;Aliens guy&quot;, except the setting has things like Fair Folk and Sidereals, so the Lunars don't really stand out even in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T04:29:56-08:00","id":789199,"title":"","content":"I forget which edition it was said that Lunars were created to be the consorts of the Solars, So what exactly was the purpose of the shapeshifting, you might ask?<br /> <br /> I always found this explanation a bit sad because it means that in a solar/lunar marriage there IS a hierarchy, and it's by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T04:37:21-08:00","id":789201,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, that's something that's no longer the case in 3rd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T05:18:18-08:00","id":789209,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about the nature of the Exalted in general, and it's got me considering some new things about Lunars.<br /> <br /> For instance... not all Exalted are function oriented the way Sidereals are, they're not brought into an actually institution and given a codified position with a mandate and a set of duties and a standard operating procedure, and powers that are tools to engage with those functions, but I would say that pretty much any Exalted are Chosen to fulfill something. For the Solars, it's not simply a matter of being powerful people who can use that power for whatever; it's about being a passionate, motivated person, the kind of people who are already inclined to pursue things that are grand, that bring changes, and being appointed to the role of a culture hero. The people who are Chosen as Solars are the people who, by their character or their ambitions, will protect and guide the world. They're not infallible in how they do this so they can make mistakes or have regrets or be criticized, and it's not necessarily something they'll do at all times, and their methods may not always be palatable to us (so you can have a Nobunaga figure who is motivated by things according to ending an extended period of warring states, which still entails burning down temples filled with civilians), but it's there in the DNA of what Solars do.<br /> <br /> That's the impression I get from looking back at an excerpt from a Grabowski outline, and I think it may be something they're subtly emphasizing throughout this Edition. Certainly, this corebook contains fairly overt reference to the idea of Solars as heroes.<br /> <br /> The way I've been thinking about it is that Solars are a lot like the Avatar from the show (particularly in how nobody seems to ever assume that being the most powerful person in the world might lead any given Avatar to try taking over everything).<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that even with Solars, you've got people who will be doing particular kinds of things, it's not just &quot;you're powerful now, do as you please with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, on to Lunars.<br /> <br /> I already brought up the idea that Lunars are Chosen for character first and then develop their own functions later. The idea of Luna rewarding or resonating with a certain kind of person, a person who has broken past some kind of constraint or confinement*. It's a power that reflects the character and circumstance in which it was granted, but it's also wild and furious, and has needed to be bound to some purpose.<br /> <br /> In the First Age, this was based off of cleaving to the Solar Exalted, with Castes formed to the purpose of assisting them. We'll have to wait to see how this goes, but my assumption is that this would take a form of &quot;Caste that complements Solar or covers their limitations or weaknesses&quot; rather than &quot;lesser version of Solar's Caste that is fit to be a sidekick&quot;. I think if one views Solars in terms of that culture hero role (which is something greater than the characteristics of their Charms, so you can have Melee Charms that are solely about being more powerful in fighting and still assume that this is always in the hands of somebody in the culture hero role), then I think that distinction alone can create a different picture of what Lunars are and were before Charms even enter into it (and so can more comfortably settle in to some Charms that are kind of... straightforward as being powerful at actions).<br /> <br /> Then you've got the Second Age, in which the Solars and the Realm that Lunars were bound to is gone, and the ruling power hates them. The role afforded to that wild, furious power is how to survive and fight back against the forces arrayed against it. The Lunar is more than simply a rebel**, although rebellion might be part of the role they've assumed in this Age.<br /> <br /> But then I've got to wonder what's on the cards for Lunars if they should destroy their enemies. It can't be to take up that guiding culture hero role; apart from Holden once clearly pointing out reasons for it not fitting their character, it just goes back in the direction of them coming across as doing Solar things in a paradigm where they can't really compete with Solars.<br /> <br /> Then I think about some statements in the core, some comments from the developer (mostly about Lunar pursuit of freedom and that idea of changing themselves rather than the world) and some of my own changing ideas about Exalted, aaannnddd...<br /> <br /> I have this idea where the thing Lunars are fighting for, and may even continue fighting the Solars for, is a world in which it's possible to be comfortably Casteless. To be rewarded by Luna for that act and chaacter of escape or defiance or non-conformity or survival and then just stop with that; to not need to have a role to hold it together. To be given power, and be able to use it for basically whatever they want (with an understanding that this will entail living lives of adventure and intrigue, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YIXErFaifkA\" target=\"_blank\">using their rad powers to slice and dice their way to fame and fortune</a>, more than arbitrarily setting people on fire for fun or something). I say &quot;Casteless&quot;, but I mean that somewhat figuratively, since the description of the Castes in the core already entails a bit of the idea of them using their power for their own benefit; it's like, being a No Moon Caste Lunar doesn't necessarily mean solving mysteries as some indication of some greater cosmic function or fulfilling some role, or require them to do it in some particularly distinctive manner, it's just... the thing that you want, or the way of getting things that you want. On that note, it seems as though the vestiges of that idea of being powerful in a way that you are ultimately free is also something partially expressed by how the core presents the Lunars, in things such as references to ones outside the Silver Pact and one of the selling points given for them.<br /> <br /> So I think that's part of what a Lunar is; something on the way to being really the only Exalted who are <i>for</i> nothing but themselves (and that as a thing without judgement).<br /> <br /> * Incidentally, if I characterise Solars as people who can be turned into culture heroes, that alone can provide a sound, if subtle, difference between them and Lunars.<br /> ** Similar to the Solars, but being another point made in that Grabowski outline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T05:50:16-08:00","id":789217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget which edition it was said that Lunars were created to be the consorts of the Solars, So what exactly was the purpose of the shapeshifting, you might ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way to look at it is not &quot;Lunars were made to be consorts to the Solars, and shapeshifting helps with that&quot;, but rather that Lunars are shapeshifters who were made to be consorts to the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found this explanation a bit sad because it means that in a solar/lunar marriage there IS a hierarchy, and it's by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. Even if we assume they stick to that, I think it can be a hierarchy in the same way a Solar is placed above their tyrant lizard familiar, in a way that doesn't exactly detract from it being a four metre tall killing machine. Still, hierarchy does not necessarily imply functional power dynamics; it's not as if there's never been a consort who wielded significant influence over their supposedly stronger spouse, or even outright dominated them.<br /> <br /> Besides, that's all in the past; what Lunars are <i>not</i> being written as now is people who will naturally fall back into that role the first time they meet a Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, that's something that's no longer the case in 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part? Because, I mean, page 46: &quot;The Lunar Exalted were created to be the Solars\u2019 seconds, their spouses, and the sacred guardians of the Old Realm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T06:34:11-08:00","id":789227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789199#post789199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget which edition it was said that Lunars were created to be the consorts of the Solars, So what exactly was the purpose of the shapeshifting, you might ask?<br /> <br /> I always found this explanation a bit sad because it means that in a solar/lunar marriage there IS a hierarchy, and it's by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition Exalted was supposed to be the secret prehistory of the cWoD line back when Exalted was first being launched. Thus each exalt type reflected one of the Main cWoD lines at the time. The Lunars were the analogs to the Werewolf: The Apocalypse werewolves and other shifter breeds. Strangely enough the Solars were the Hunter analog and the Dragon-Blooded were connected to the Kuei-Jin, while the Sidereals were the mages and the abyssal were the cainite vampires.<br /> <br /> The sun and moon consort concept was a staple the myths and legends that Exalted was drew upon for that old school legendary feel. Thus the source materials they drew upon had such hierarchy in place to begin with before the game designers ever got their hands on it.<br /> <br /> So many of the original design concepts make sense when viewed from the perspective of being connected to old world of darkness lines or draw direct inspiration from things like the labors of Hercules or the adventures of Enkidu &amp; Gilgamesh. But once they started moving away from those sources and delving more into distancing Exalted as a stand alone line and gaining more and more inspiration from things like anime, the original designs made less and less sense, but you had to keep them to maintain a degree of consistency between editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:23:34-08:00","id":789241,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with the Thousand Streams River Project was that MoEP: Lunars drank its own kool aid (it did this constantly) and couldn't see the potential immorality of this kind of society shaping especially the instances when they're hard coding personal beliefs and prejudices into the culture. Then there's the question of how they deal with reformers, again we can only guess how many people have been brainwashed or outright disposed of because they didn't see the bigger picture and the Lunar couldn't risk bringing them in on the plan.<br /> <br /> Without this kind of thought the TSR couldn't offer a unique Lunar playstyle and it simply became an unsatisfactory answer of what the non-insane elders were doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:25:26-08:00","id":789244,"title":"","content":"Lemme preface this by saying that I'm grateful to be a part of such an invested community; this thread has given me a lot of ideas for my lunar games, and along with Irked's conversion, has helped me ensure that Lunars will get to play a neat role in my current game, which has otherwise focused exclusively on Solars and the Dragonblooded (with some Abyssals thrown in, but the Solars don't know that yet).<br /> <br /> Lunars.<br /> <br /> I only started getting really into Exalted around about a year or so ago, well into the timeframe within which Morke and Holden were writing long posts about the issues they've had in past editions, and a little bit about their vision for their place in the setting moving forward. So, I'm approaching this subject with only a faint idea, for example, of how Ma-Ha-Suchi was depicted in 2E, which I take to be bad somehow.<br /> <br /> To me, Lunars in and of themselves conjure an <i>awesome </i>collection of images. The strength of an enormous man-beast hybrid, rippling and surging with muscle. Razor-keen senses and instincts. A thousand faces in a thousand places. The wealth of imagery and themes of the animal world tied to ancient cunning and centuries-long foresight. I find animals pretty mind-boggling as it is (blame my biology training), and the thought of adding Essence to the already insane capabilities incipient in the natural world is exciting. Wise shamans, peerless hunters, slippery tricksters. Physicality.<br /> <br /> Then there's how they fit into Creation as a whole. I've personally always enjoyed the idea of them being the largest, most effective spy and guerilla force in the history of Creation. Powerful individually; in some cases, such as Raksi, Ma-Ha-Suchi, and Sha'a Oka even powerful enough to wrest and keep territory, but generally outmatched by both numbers and inherited technological capability. Living out the the dynamic tension between surviving the Realm and defeating the Realm while wrestling with an ancient, terrible bond. I can understand why some would hate to play second fiddle to Solars/Abyssals/Infernals, but I've never really been bugged by this because I think it opens up a lot of neat stories involving re-brokering these power dynamics in the forging of a new age. Or hell, even going with it, and playing a loyal, die-hard partner to an unstoppable, occasionally power-mad Solar. Or redeeming a nihilistic Abyssal (or joining them, as a Lunar of Death!). And if you want to hold onto having a loyal Lunar mate as a Solar (something which I think people generally agree is awesome), that dynamic is going to <i>have</i> to stay a part of the setting in Lunar games<i>. </i><br /> <br /> If you want to play an unstoppable general or an irresistible orator, Solars already provide that role, and I think it's unfair to critique Lunars for not being that (which is a subtext that I've seen come up a number of times when people complain about them). In terms of raw power, while they may be behind Solars and associated brands on average, any military commander or historian will tell you that adaptability and flexibility, the hallmarks of Lunars, outweigh raw strength as often as not. Hell, it takes the combined strength of the Dragonblooded empire -and- the Sidereals to maintain a delicate stalemate, and even that with several large Lunar dominions still in place. I don't get the impression from their write-ups in this edition at least that they've been sitting on their hands/tentacles/claws, waiting for the Solars to show up. I get the impression that they've been the single biggest problem for the most powerful people in the world for <i>centuries. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:50:32-08:00","id":789257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem with the Thousand Streams River Project was that MoEP: Lunars drank its own kool aid (it did this constantly) and couldn't see the potential immorality of this kind of society shaping especially the instances when they're hard coding personal beliefs and prejudices into the culture. Then there's the question of how they deal with reformers, again we can only guess how many people have been brainwashed or outright disposed of because they didn't see the bigger picture and the Lunar couldn't risk bringing them in on the plan.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a lot to say about the Thousand Streams River, but I think I can get to my most essential issue by looking back at when I was first starting to get interested in Exalted, and reading all of the Charms and stuff on the wiki, and finding the little staggers and stutters that were created in my summary of Lunars. &quot;The Lunars are mighty shapeshifters! .... Which they apply to social engineering... because you're ideally suited to manipulating a society when you can... hide out as a bird... I guess? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Wait, Solar Socialize?</span>&quot; See also their Charms, and the whole Stewards thing. Honestly, with this new perspective, I'm even rather happy to let go of the idea that some high-minded Lunar elders have an agenda of turning human societies back into a forager structure that they view as more moral and sustainable; that can just be a thing in the heart of one returned Lawgiver, who then crosses paths with another one who thinks that renewing the world requires all of the cities, and then they can fight it out with all of the ambiguity and disagreement without one needing to be a crude villain or appeal to contemporary anxieties that all authority is corruptible and untrustworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T09:27:15-08:00","id":789275,"title":"","content":"Our problem with the Lunars isn't that they're less powerful than Solars. Its that they're the least powerful Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> It was supposed to be;<br /> Solars&gt;Lunars=Siderials&gt;Alchemicals&gt;&gt;Terrestrials<br /> What we got was;<br /> Solars&gt;Siderials&gt;Alchemicals&gt;Lunars&gt;Terrestrials(t he last greater than is barely)<br /> Although 2e kept adding more stuff with supplements so it became more;<br /> Solars&gt;Siderials&gt;Alchemicals=Lunars&gt;&gt;Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Its almost as if Luna got her exalted last. Like Gaia was already on board with the gods' revolution 'cause the other primordials kept messing up Creation(an extension of Gaia). It was originally US, the Maidens, Nox, Autochthon and Gaia fighting the war. Luna was left out because she was an outsider who seemed too mercurial in disposition to trust. Then when Nox betrayed the group they brought in Luna, but the war had already started and the Lunars had no clearly defined role. Worse, they were mistrusted and were bonded to the Solars to keep them in line. Nevertheless, the Lunars were able to act as Jacks-of-all-Trades, fulfilling any role as needed.<br /> <br /> Wait..., (looks at post), did I just write a better Primordial War back-story? ...nah.<br /> <br /> This is all largely due to the overall story though. Even in continuity, the Lunars feel tacked-on. They don't contribute much to history. We're talking about a level of power where forming a nation should be relatively easy. Yet it took a group of Lunars to conquer a small continent. (as unenthusiastically as possible) \u201cWoop-dee-doo, Basil.\u201d This minute impact on the setting does little to allay this.<br /> Heck, the entries on Lunars in the new core book make them look more like the \u201cChosen of Animals\u201d than ever. Only their Excellencies make them seem Celestial and, to be frank (he's in my Heartsblood list ;P ), that's not enough. The Lunars need to be important to the setting and powerful enough to do it. More than that they need a properly Celestial theme from which this power arises.<br /> <br /> Anywho, I've done too many rants on this already. So, last one. I'll move on to other things now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T09:55:50-08:00","id":789283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789257#post789257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's a lot to say about the Thousand Streams River, but I think I can get to my most essential issue by looking back at when I was first starting to get interested in Exalted, and reading all of the Charms and stuff on the wiki, and finding the little staggers and stutters that were created in my summary of Lunars. &quot;The Lunars are mighty shapeshifters! .... Which they apply to social engineering... because you're ideally suited to manipulating a society when you can... hide out as a bird... I guess? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Wait, Solar Socialize?</span>&quot; See also their Charms, and the whole Stewards thing. Honestly, with this new perspective, I'm even rather happy to let go of the idea that some high-minded Lunar elders have an agenda of turning human societies back into a forager structure that they view as more moral and sustainable; that can just be a thing in the heart of one returned Lawgiver, who then crosses paths with another one who thinks that renewing the world requires all of the cities, and then they can fight it out with all of the ambiguity and disagreement without one needing to be a crude villain or appeal to contemporary anxieties that all authority is corruptible and untrustworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I prefer the execution of the War Dominions because I consider them more honest about what Exalts who aren't hundreds of years old get out of the situation while still leaving room for Lunars who genuinely care about their people and espouse the way of life they live. Aum-Ashatra for example seems like he's created something that has value beyond what damage it can do to the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:30:33-08:00","id":789303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet it took a group of Lunars to conquer a small continent. (as unenthusiastically as possible) \u201cWoop-dee-doo, Basil.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div> Already I feel you're not arguing in good faith. Still, to the extent that this warrents response; yes, it does take a fair number of Lunars to fight the Realm, with its many Dragon Blooded and ancient weapons, for control over what has to be one of their highest priority possessions in the Threshold (between the cultural significance, the strategic value of it as a gateway to the lucrative West, and that whole &quot;pilgrimage that improves chance of next child being Exalted&quot; thing. Certainly, I'm not sure how one reads &quot;Lunars of singular zealotry&quot; as indicating lack of enthusiasm. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">minute impact on the setting</div> </div> </div> </div> For &quot;minute impact on the setting&quot; read &quot;outer rim of Creation is a ring of knives against which the Realm has to continuously deploy expensive military ventures&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the entries on Lunars in the new core book make them look more like the \u201cChosen of Animals\u201d than ever.</div> </div> </div> </div> When did people stop being impressed enough with animals to stop making legends about them? &quot;Jeez, what was the big deal of Heracles to the Greeks and Romans, all he did was fight a lion, some birds and a swamp lizard. Any liquered up hillbilly could do that with a shotgun at the zoo.&quot; <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only their Excellencies make them seem Celestial</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a clarifying definition of &quot;Celestial&quot; lurking somewhere behind this sentiment, but I don't yet have enough data to extrapolate it. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the execution of the War Dominions because I consider them more honest about what Exalts who aren't hundreds of years old get out of the situation while still leaving room for Lunars who genuinely care about their people and espouse the way of life they live.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find the dominions to be a good example of an Exalt applying their powers in a scenario, without needing to make that scenario exemplery of what they are. Indeed, the idea that a Lunar can effectively create and command such a force without making such a thing a direct function of their powers or nature could be taken as a more subtle instance of Lunar versatility. The idea that Lunars are commanding barbarian kingdoms against their enemies not because they're the barbarian Exalted, but because that's what largely works in the scenario in which their enemies have forced them. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aum-Ashatra for example seems like he's created something that has value beyond what damage it can do to the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div> It makes me wonder if people who have read the whole thing as unforgiveably callous stopped reading at some point, or just continued with a bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T11:26:16-08:00","id":789333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789283#post789283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aum-Ashatra for example seems like he's created something that has value beyond what damage it can do to the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mountain of the Spider King is my favorite Lunar Dominion of those we've seen because of this. The Caul is still really interesting, and steeped in a lot of cool religious and ideological motivations/themes for both Lunars and Dragonblooded, but Aum-Ashatra's claimed territory is a fantastic show of what Lunars might be able to achieve in a productive and sustainable way rather than just being focused or reliant on predation of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-19-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:50:54-08:00","id":789375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789303#post789303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Jeez, what was the big deal of Heracles to the Greeks and Romans, all he did was fight a lion, some birds and a swamp lizard. Any liquered up hillbilly could do that with a shotgun at the zoo.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh ... yes ... and and the lion and the birds and the lizard were in the story and got killed as the antagonists they were - they had no agenda. It's extremely rare to have animals in myths which are protagonists because of their animalness. Anansi and Mantis and Inchneumon might be animals, but in their myths they act just like humans. Simba might be a king of the lions, but the story is not &quot;that is how lions behave in Africa&quot;, the story is &quot;Hamlet as told with animals&quot;. So I don't really understand why Lunars seem to be limited so strongly to &quot;like animals in nature&quot; instead of being &quot;like animals in fables&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another problem I see with Lunars is the definition of &quot;best survivors&quot; mostly as &quot;can adjust to any circumstance&quot;. I would argue that - at least in our world - the best survivors are humans simpley because we don't adjust to the circumstances but adjust the circumstances to us. This is partly related to the strong predator/barbarian theme of the Lunars and the inherent limitation of this: predators are often the weakest part of an ecosystem and rely on prey (or metaphorically: civilization to plunder) and die out without them, while the &quot;weak prey&quot; can survive on its own.<br /> Of course, changing Lunars from ... let's call it &quot;reactive survivors&quot; to &quot;active survivors&quot; and supporting this with charms would turn them from &quot;inwards&quot; Exalted to &quot;outwards&quot; Exalted and apparently the designers don't want to do that. But in my opinion this means that Lunars are inherently limited.<br /> Well, yea, the Spider King is apparently such an &quot;outwards Lunar&quot;, but he seems so ... off ... and different to other Lunars in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my group has decided on &quot;Lunars can be anything they want&quot;. Similar like Luna has the othermoons with their own themes, the Lunar in our group can chose any theme he wants and incorporate it in his charmset. The number of themes he can have (and in more crunchy terms: the roles he can fill/support in the party) is limited by Essence and his commitment - he is not able to dabble into anything a little, but instead choses a handful of focusses which he expresses through as many attributes as possible.<br /> Of course, this does not fit in any way with the official stance on Lunars and how their splatbook will look. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:53:31-08:00","id":789381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789257#post789257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's a lot to say about the Thousand Streams River, but I think I can get to my most essential issue by looking back at when I was first starting to get interested in Exalted, and reading all of the Charms and stuff on the wiki, and finding the little staggers and stutters that were created in my summary of Lunars. &quot;The Lunars are mighty shapeshifters! .... Which they apply to social engineering... because you're ideally suited to manipulating a society when you can... hide out as a bird... I guess? <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Wait, Solar Socialize?</span>&quot; See also their Charms, and the whole Stewards thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the proviso this is all about something I haven't read for a while, I feel like I want to say this is a lot less dumb than you make it sound. The Lunars were, I think, stressed as the champions of adaptability, from which an understanding of how and why societies can change and then the Thousand Streams River naturally unfolds. They were presented clearly, I think, as the Exalted who would have the highest, most natural and best understanding of this idea.<br /> <br /> Did their Charms actually back this up? Perhaps not. Is this a pulp fantasy enough thing for Exalted, or is it too &quot;sci fi&quot;? Perhaps not (but then if it's not, Solars using Socialize to do a variation on the theme sure as fuck wouldn't be either, so there's that).<br /> <br /> (The TSR is defensible on nothing more than it not being just another avenue of presenting a setting where Exalted splats are at one another's throats (splatism). Good or not, it has that. In theory, I'd also like to say that, as a notion, which may or may not hold up under scrutiny, I like the fact that on some level all the Exalted splats really should be are designed with the kind of depth that they can think deeply about changing and shaping human societies for what they believe to be the better, and can act as guides in how to achieve that, in real terms, replete with all moral hazard.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T14:31:45-08:00","id":789428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789303#post789303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Already I feel you're not arguing in good faith. Still, to the extent that this warrents response; yes, it does take a fair number of Lunars to fight the Realm, with its many Dragon Blooded and ancient weapons, for control over what has to be one of their highest priority possessions in the Threshold (between the cultural significance, the strategic value of it as a gateway to the lucrative West, and that whole &quot;pilgrimage that improves chance of next child being Exalted&quot; thing. Certainly, I'm not sure how one reads &quot;Lunars of singular zealotry&quot; as indicating lack of enthusiasm.<br /> For &quot;minute impact on the setting&quot; read &quot;outer rim of Creation is a ring of knives against which the Realm has to continuously deploy expensive military ventures&quot;.<br /> When did people stop being impressed enough with animals to stop making legends about them? &quot;Jeez, what was the big deal of Heracles to the Greeks and Romans, all he did was fight a lion, some birds and a swamp lizard. Any liquered up hillbilly could do that with a shotgun at the zoo.&quot;<br /> There's a clarifying definition of &quot;Celestial&quot; lurking somewhere behind this sentiment, but I don't yet have enough data to extrapolate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, my statement may have been overly throwaway. However, the Caul was added to give the Lunars something to achieve without having to change the plot. The difficulty it was to achieve doesn't make the Realm look any more powerful, they already rule most of the world. It just makes the Lunars look weak because it took a group of them to conquer an area only slightly bigger than the Bull of the North's. I'm not saying there's a lack of enthusiasm. I'm saying there's a lack of power.<br /> <br /> The Roman Empire had a similar ring. Can you name any of the Germanic &quot;Barbarian&quot; Tribes that constantly threatened<i> them</i> for centuries without looking it up? Also discounting the Visigoths who sacked Rome after the capital was moved to Byzantium (then renamed Constantinople) and cut off support to the western empire. There is little evidence of this threat in creation thus further weakening the perception of Lunars.<br /> <br /> Animals are an excellent source for folklore, just like the elements and elementals, and on the same level. Animals can be cool and powerful, but they're <b>Terrestrial</b>. I have no problem with there being Terrestrial Chosen of Animals, but that isn't <b>Celestial</b>. The excellencies convey the power of a Celestial by allowing the Lunars to have two Attributes of dice added(if they stunt it), but even then it doesn't convey a theme beyond animals. (Though to answer your question; we stopped making legends about them when we invented guns. No, really.)<br /> <br /> Basically, Lunars don't have the power or majesty of the heavens. They have the power and majesty of the bear, the tiger and the snake. While that is cool. It isn't Lunar.<br /> <br /> What we're trying to get to is the central theme of Lunars and all we have is shape-shifting and animals. This is, again, a <b>Terrestrial</b> threat not a <b>Celestial</b> one. THAT is why we're worried. We want Lunars to be Celestials and for two editions they haven't been. The new core book doesn't give any more to the Lunars than previous editions and takes some things away. This gives the <u>impression</u> that Lunars have lost power. The Caul is meant to alleviate that but doesn't succeed. With what I've seen so far, I'm just hoping that Lunars make it to being as powerful as Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> Dang it, I said I wouldn't do that anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T15:03:25-08:00","id":789440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh ... yes ... and and the lion and the birds and the lizard were in the story and got killed as the antagonists they were - they had no agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, because that's the side to focus on. Why, I just know that any time I see somebody advocate, say, Jason as an inspiration for Solars, they're just <i>aching</i> to play a character who gets crushed under a mast in their first scene, and even if they weren't they would have no recourse, because putting the capabilities of Jason to any other end is just impossible. I suppose it will be a sad day for Lunars fans when they're given Charms for horrific claws or indestructible hide with clauses such as &quot;buying this means that a Solar is going to strangle you to death in the next scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand why Lunars seem to be limited so strongly to &quot;like animals in nature&quot; instead of being &quot;like animals in fables&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not limited to, inspired by. And not even &quot;animals in nature&quot;, more &quot;animals as they spark the imagination with their diversity and capabilities&quot;. It's still not even capturing the full picture, since there's more nuance to what the developers have said than &quot;you'll get Charms to aid crafting by being able to build like a beaver&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> problem I see with Lunars is the definition of &quot;best survivors&quot; mostly as &quot;can adjust to any circumstance&quot;. I would argue that - at least in our world - the best survivors are humans simpley because we don't adjust to the circumstances but adjust the circumstances to us.</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks like semantics. I don't even think Lunars should be about &quot;best survivors&quot; so much as &quot;survival suffuses their experience&quot; (in much the same way that Sidereals are better off with having the prophet stuff strewn throughout their abilities and experience rather than treating it as a niche to be superior in), but whether or not the term is being applied as you would apply it doesn't seem to speak to its merits or lack thereof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">changing Lunars from ... let's call it &quot;reactive survivors&quot; to &quot;active survivors&quot; and supporting this with charms would turn them from &quot;inwards&quot; Exalted to &quot;outwards&quot; Exalted and apparently the designers don't want to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a view that discounts the whole shapeshifting thing. I mean, yes, we need to do things like build insulated houses and make warm clothing from certain kinds of animal hair and skins (and then sunthetic fibers) because we can't adapt to grow our own fur. Lunars do not have that issue. My image of a Lunar who can adapt to survive in scenarios in which enemies can't follow them is one who turns into a falcon and flies to the top of a mountain where no Wyld Hunt can follow, or runs down into a series of caves in which the majority of enemies would quickly become lost and blind, assuming whatever qualities will allow them to best acquire what nutrition is needed wherever they wind up. It's by no means comprehensive, it's not even exactly about a play experience, but it gives a sense of what it might mean for the Lunar character to be one that confounds their enemies by being able to go to ground in places where they just can't be followed. To be a Lunar is to live in a world of asteroid fields in opposition to people who would be crazy to follow you in, where you don't even need to be driven out by giant rock worms, because the giant rock worm is you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Spider King is apparently such an &quot;outwards Lunar&quot;, but he seems so ... off ... and different to other Lunars in the corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Because his particular approach to the might and cunning of beasts involves a web-based detection system?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say this is a lot less dumb than you make it sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it was an impression being gleaned from short wiki summaries. I'm trying to get across my impression of the time of it having gaps, and my own difficulty of figuring out how it was pieced together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars were, I think, stressed as the champions of adaptability, from which an understanding of how and why societies can change and then the Thousand Streams River naturally unfolds.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an interpretation, that makes even less sense to me. Do the way Lunars adapt and the way societies change really resemble one another much?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TSR is defensible on nothing more than it not being just another avenue of presenting a setting where Exalted splats are at one another's throats (splatism).</div> </div> </div> </div>If this was the case to be made, I feel as though a comic featuring a Lunar complaining about Solars was a bad way to go. Which is to say, given the whole angle of &quot;make the world not need the Exalted&quot;, being at their throats seems to at least be implicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, I'd also like to say that, as a notion, which may or may not hold up under scrutiny, I like the fact that on some level all the Exalted splats really should be are designed with the kind of depth that they can think deeply about changing and shaping human societies for what they believe to be the better, and can act as guides in how to achieve that, in real terms, replete with all moral hazard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the problem with this is that it's the kind of thing where you ultimately get each type of Exalted as being an advocate for a kind of Hat for a society to wear (so you get things like people talking about Solars as advocates for a particular kind of civilization, say, urbanized and with complex stratification, compared to the Lunars as a kind of tribal one and... I'm not even sure for the rest), which would seem to have a few issues to me. The most obvious is that it would grate against the rest of the game's structure in which the Exalted are supposed to be notably different from one another, as well as their hierarchy (which would also mean you kind of bias in favour of what the Solars advocate, given their advantage), which was done to avoid the pitfalls of them being reskins of the same thing. It also looks to me like something fairly shallow, because depth wouldn't support its necessary rigidity. There's also the matter of how, while part of the attitude of the game is remaking the world, this is more a matter of stories resulting from the application of mechanics rather than mechanics themselves, because it's not a management sim, and it would otherwise be something that kind of leaves a character focusing on something like Melee out. That leads into the final point; that the Solar Exalted are at the core of the game, meaning they're at the forefront of fulfilling that central narrative premise of &quot;passionate, motivated people have the capacity to change the world&quot;; I think it would represent a failing of that premise being used by the core of the game to say &quot;actually, you can only do it in a particular way&quot;. At this point, I don't see a compelling reason to make the story in which primitivist advocate Solar and urban Solar (and possibly their dispute) are not equally valid. A central tension of the game is the world holding its breath to see what kind of world the returned Lawgivers will make, and I think that's diminished if they're only given a limited selection; I also don't think it helps the credibility of the other ones to say that they have their own subsets of world changing that they're naturals to, but have either failed to implement, or the implementation.* <br /> <br /> I talked about a difficulty in grasping the Thousand Streams River from the surface level, but with this perspective I have a new sense of what is wrong with it. Namely, that in trying to figure out something for the Lunars to have been doing, it took a premise covertly at the heart of the central narrative of Exalted (&quot;returning heroes to renew hope and justice in the world&quot;), made it overt, overly technical, and in the hands of characters to whom it was not suited and, worst of all, couched it in terms of the cynicism that the premise was supposed to be against.<br /> <br /> The Thousand Streams River said &quot;you have to remake the world into something in which the Exalted have no place, because their reign is illegitimate and unjust&quot;, and the game just doesn't really work if it assumes that of the Exalted. The game is supposed to grab people's attention and give them direction for play with the idea that they're playing characters whose return to power can be truly hopeful and righteous if they succeed. If it creates a strong advocacy for the idea that the characters you're given to play are not legitimate, then what are you supposed to do with them?<br /> <br /> That, I think, may be the biggest issue with the Thousand Streams River; its core premises are directly contradictory.<br /> <br /> * Yes, I know there are people who will look at the idea that the other Exalted are not naturals to the task of guiding and renewing the world as a suggestion that they are worthless and incompetent compared to the Solars, to whom they are obligated. To that I say: when the premise of the game is that you're coming into a world at the end of history, without hope or fresh impetus, then I feel that to say that the other Exalted should have equal facility with that Solar narrative is to render them failures and incompetent, and that to say that this isn't part of what they do frees them of some of the potential strain to their credibility. I mean, that the world has fallen so far in the Second Age still reflects badly on the other Exalted, but in terms of their interactions and certain key decisions and even just their luck, not on things pertinent to the means by which you play them. To play a Lunar as focused on something other than the task of renewing the world is to be able to play a Lunar who can do those things well. Not everybody needs to be a culture hero to guide the world, and under other circumstances the world could have done without culture heroes. Even placing that responsibility on the returning Solars need not make others subservient to them; not if the Solars can be guided or constrained by the advice or opposition of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:00:16-08:00","id":789457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, I just know that any time I see somebody advocate, say, Jason as an inspiration for Solars, they're just <i>aching</i> to play a character who gets crushed under a mast in their first scene, and even if they weren't they would have no recourse, because putting the capabilities of Jason to any other end is just impossible. I suppose it will be a sad day for Lunars fans when they're given Charms for horrific claws or indestructible hide with clauses such as &quot;buying this means that a Solar is going to strangle you to death in the next scene&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, great, we're back to snark. So please tell me what the great and awesome character and story inspiration is you get from the Nemean Lion that is not &quot;dangerous in a fight&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand: Don't. This will be my last post in this thread anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still not even capturing the full picture, since there's more nuance to what the developers have said than &quot;you'll get Charms to aid crafting by being able to build like a beaver&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that mean we can hope for &quot;I can organize a nation of millions of people and build awesome infrastructure for them&quot;-charms based on termites. And for the whalesong- and beedance-charms that allows to create really awesome music and performances. Oh, wait, no ... that would step on the toes of Solars, most likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be a Lunar is to live in a world of asteroid fields in opposition to people who would be crazy to follow you in, where you don't even need to be driven out by giant rock worms, because the giant rock worm is you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, the great escape-guy who can remove himself from society and active play whenever he wants. Yea, I really enjoyed that retelling of ESB in which they never had to leave the asteroid anymore. Really awesome how that helped to build a new republic.<br /> <br /> And that was my turn at snark and with that I bow out of this thread. And most likely of this board.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">I wish I hadn't forgotten the snark and badwrongfun-isms which made me quit posting in this board on the old forum.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/643-taliesin","name":"Taliesin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:16:12-08:00","id":789461,"title":"","content":"Talking about what Exalted are is a lot easier if you get rid of meaningless words like &quot;terrestrial&quot; and &quot;celestial.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:18:49-08:00","id":789463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789428#post789428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, my statement may have been overly throwaway. However, the Caul was added to give the Lunars something to achieve without having to change the plot. The difficulty it was to achieve doesn't make the Realm look any more powerful, they already rule most of the world. It just makes the Lunars look weak because it took a group of them to conquer an area only slightly bigger than the Bull of the North's. I'm not saying there's a lack of enthusiasm. I'm saying there's a lack of power.<br /> <br /> The Roman Empire had a similar ring. Can you name any of the Germanic &quot;Barbarian&quot; Tribes that constantly threatened<i> them</i> for centuries without looking it up? Also discounting the Visigoths who sacked Rome after the capital was moved to Byzantium (then renamed Constantinople) and cut off support to the western empire. There is little evidence of this threat in creation thus further weakening the perception of Lunars.<br /> <br /> Animals are an excellent source for folklore, just like the elements and elementals, and on the same level. Animals can be cool and powerful, but they're <b>Terrestrial</b>. I have no problem with there being Terrestrial Chosen of Animals, but that isn't <b>Celestial</b>. The excellencies convey the power of a Celestial by allowing the Lunars to have two Attributes of dice added(if they stunt it), but even then it doesn't convey a theme beyond animals. (Though to answer your question; we stopped making legends about them when we invented guns. No, really.)<br /> <br /> Basically, Lunars don't have the power or majesty of the heavens. They have the power and majesty of the bear, the tiger and the snake. While that is cool. It isn't Lunar.<br /> <br /> What we're trying to get to is the central theme of Lunars and all we have is shape-shifting and animals. This is, again, a <b>Terrestrial</b> threat not a <b>Celestial</b> one. THAT is why we're worried. We want Lunars to be Celestials and for two editions they haven't been. The new core book doesn't give any more to the Lunars than previous editions and takes some things away. This gives the <u>impression</u> that Lunars have lost power. The Caul is meant to alleviate that but doesn't succeed. With what I've seen so far, I'm just hoping that Lunars make it to being as powerful as Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> Dang it, I said I wouldn't do that anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that something can be instrinsically,essentially, and inescapably said to be &quot;Terrestrial&quot; or &quot;Celestial&quot;. This goes double if you're the one setting the dials; you could just set the concept of &quot;beasts&quot; very low, but there's no inherent or vital reason to do so in a game, particularly one in which a human can punch a divine being in the face and reasonably expect to break the entity in question. If you can expect that this is what the underlying assumptions of the setting paint as &quot;natural human prowess, at the highest possible power level&quot;, then it shouldn't be a stretch to have Lunar powers involve mauling gods with their talons or tearing them apart like a tiger catching a small deer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:37:38-08:00","id":789473,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I went over several ways to articulate that point about the Greek monsters thing, some of which were more direct and didn't have snark. Obviously, I followed the wrong impulse. I won't edit the post, because I won't act like I'm trying to revise myself to something more palatable, but for what it's worth, I apologise for not conducting myself better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T17:49:43-08:00","id":789513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taliesin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789375#post789375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, my group has decided on &quot;Lunars can be anything they want&quot;. Similar like Luna has the othermoons with their own themes, the Lunar in our group can chose any theme he wants and incorporate it in his charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that would <b>so </b>not work for me. A charmset consisting of a bunch of disparate whatever-you-want themes sounds terrible for my taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T18:35:52-08:00","id":789538,"title":"","content":"Personally I think Lunars would be best positioned as those who bridge the wyld amd creation. The scouts, emissaries, explorers, who go before the Solars. They are fringe dwellers and hunters by purpose, not by default, and their greatest strength is their immunity to the wyld. <br /> <br /> As for them being the least powerful, i think that's an unfortunate effect of meta gaming in design. The original writers wanted each exalt type to function mechanically different from each other and lunars, whose charms are attached to attributes, got the un-playtested short end of the stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T18:58:16-08:00","id":789559,"title":"","content":"I think there are issues with defining Lunars by immunity to the Wyld from things such as the likelihood that that's the kind of thing that would only be encompassed in about two or three Charms (even if it wasn't flatly made by their tattoos), and the fact that there's not a lot to do with the Wyld, especially when the game is going to be focused on more human drama that would keep most focus on Creation. That said, the Third Edition write-up does seem to make it a significant part of their repetoire; they can use the Wyld as a safe haven, and that probably helps in a lot of their endeavours, but the thing itself does not have much interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T20:05:20-08:00","id":789575,"title":"","content":"I think the Wyld is more a dangerous place which Lunars have made their home because of their adaptability and cunning, rather than something which defines them as Exalts.<br /> Like how the Blessed Isle is the base of the Dragonblood, and so has a great cultural effect on them, but their charms are not about civilisation or Empire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T20:46:50-08:00","id":789586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789461#post789461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about what Exalted are is a lot easier if you get rid of meaningless words like &quot;terrestrial&quot; and &quot;celestial.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I could respond to all the other posts, but this was said..., by a Dev.<br /> ...<br /> That answers all my questions. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T20:53:16-08:00","id":789589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789575#post789575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Wyld is more a dangerous place which Lunars have made their home because of their adaptability and cunning, rather than something which defines them as Exalts.<br /> Like how the Blessed Isle is the base of the Dragonblood, and so has a great cultural effect on them, but their charms are not about civilisation or Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they haven't made it their home. EX3 has them staying in Creation, where the things they care about are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T22:08:31-08:00","id":789611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789586#post789586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could respond to all the other posts, but this was said..., by a Dev.<br /> ...<br /> That answers all my questions. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Last I saw Mr. Vance was a writer, not a developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T23:29:25-08:00","id":789628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789461#post789461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about what Exalted are is a lot easier if you get rid of meaningless words like &amp;quot;terrestrial&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;celestial.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As determinants of power level, at least, though this is something doubled down on in martial arts in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> As the source of their power? I think Terrestrial and Celestial are great words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T05:04:32-08:00","id":789680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789611#post789611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last I saw Mr. Vance was a writer, not a developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way it shows the thought processes being applied to the &quot;Lunars&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T05:36:14-08:00","id":789685,"title":"","content":"The term &quot;Terrestrial Exalted&quot; exists in an odd kind of nebulous space. On the one hand, it's simply the alternative term for the Dragon Blooded (and, within the setting, one that is largely archaic and unused), and basically stands as their equivalent to titles like Solar or Sidereal or Liminal Exalted. On the other, it's held up as a distinct category equivalent to the term &quot;Celestial Exalted&quot;, (which itself just really forms a convenient shorthand for Solar, Lunar and Sidereal Exalted, who are held together both for the facts that the things that they're named after are very far up, and that they have certain similar assumptions in their power and nature such as the idea that they're selected from an otherwise unknown group and can't multiply), despite the fact that it amounts to a category consisting of one. I feel the latter one is something held up more by the fanbase than the books themselves, manifesting in some rather odd qualities such as a perceived need to add additional Terrestrial Exalted or to reassign some existing one to enter it, not so much because it accomplishes anything functional but because it validates the term as a category. So the term &quot;Terrestrial Exalted&quot; is not entirely meaningless, since it still serves as a name for the Dragon Blooded (and an easier thing to use to refer to those parts of martial arts where they struggle, since it's one word), but doesn't really need to mean anything <i>beyond</i> &quot;these are the Dragon Blooded&quot; in assessing the details of any given Exalt. Now, if one were to take the tack of &quot;there are tenuous links between moon imagery and beasts&quot;, that would have less cruft, even if it's still something I would argue against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T06:44:25-08:00","id":789703,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, nevertheless, we have our answer.<br /> &quot;Lunars&quot; are the Chosen of Animals and the bonded spouses/slaves of the Solars. The writers and developers didn't leave anything out of their summary in the core book. Their charms will be dominated and overwhelmed by their shape-shifting and animal motifs. They will be driven by their rage. If you want a &quot;Lunar&quot; to travel the Wyld safely they will need moonsilver tattoos. Oh, and DBT will basically be a must for all &quot;Lunars&quot; planning on entering combat.<br /> Build your charms on those baselines and when the book comes out you won't be far off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T07:29:54-08:00","id":789716,"title":"","content":"Almost the whole thing is dreadful hyperbole, but at least could stand as an uncharitable and biased interpretation of what has been presented, but <i>this</i>: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DBT will basically be a must for all &quot;Lunars&quot; planning on entering combat </div> </div> </div> This is a <i>fabrication</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T07:34:05-08:00","id":789719,"title":"","content":"Specifically, you have a choice between using Evocations and using DBT. This is on a form by form basis; you can develop both if you want, but you can only use one of them at a time. So if you want a Lunar with a really neat magic sword, you probably won't be using DBT all that often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T07:34:27-08:00","id":789720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That leads into the final point; that the Solar Exalted are at the core of the game, meaning they're at the forefront of fulfilling that central narrative premise of &quot;passionate, motivated people have the capacity to change the world&quot;; I think it would represent a failing of that premise being used by the core of the game to say &quot;actually, you can only do it in a particular way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is supposed to grab people's attention and give them direction for play with the idea that they're playing characters whose return to power can be truly hopeful and righteous if they succeed. If it creates a strong advocacy for the idea that the characters you're given to play are not legitimate, then what are you supposed to do with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator I am not sure this is exactly what you are saying (this whole post was fairly intricate in argument), but with legitimacy, I would note the books pretty much say &quot;will destroy or save&quot; the first time the Solars are mentioned. That is the deal. The Exalted don't get a guarantee that they are a necessary or righteous force in shaping the world. Not Sidereals, not Dragonblooded, not Abyssals, not Lunars, not Alchemicals. To a degree, it up to groups to assert their belief in their characters and the splats do (again to a degree) exist to challenge one another and their stories*.<br /> <br /> The setting is not there purely to get players gassed and optimistic about what their Solar PCs can achieve and excited to see what different futures they will shape! It's built on a history tragedy and failure! And yes, questionable legitimacy. The idea that the returning Solars may only bring glorious failure and defeat is right there early.<br /> <br /> That's supposed to be a *genuine* challenge, right? One you can rise to by looking back and saying &quot;Yes, legitimately true, the Solars created a society dependent on them, then fell to decadent tyranny, one that treated the world as a canvas only for their eog and grand passions. The promise they held merely led, in the end, to blind ruin, chaos and loss. Perhaps that is in the nature of the Solar Exalted, or Exalted rule generally. But I still must try to strive to take power for what it can do, with hope of mastering demons of my nature and tendencies in my essence&quot;. Therein is the hook. <br /> <br /> Whether or not the TSR is the right way to approach it (and there are problems with it, as it stands, primarily I think of anachronism and the underlying cultural logic behind it), in many ways it is not challenging the Solar narrative and theme in a way that is not already present through the Bronze Faction (which in that instance is probably to their advantage as making an interesting splat) and writing within the 1e and 2e cores about who and what they are.<br /> <br /> I feel like there is kind of suggestion of fragility and sensitivity here that I don't understand.<br /> <br /> With whether the TSR implies that the Solars must shape the world a particular way, I don't think it ever did. At the most it implied there were tendencies there in the nature of their power and how they express it that skewed them towards a particular and in ways particularly unstable form of society, while the Lunars returned, with a specific cultural experience the Solars lacked were able to look at things differently not a mandated destiny. (Although if we're questioning and criticizing the idea that the returned Solars will have fairly narrow mandated destinies, at what can tie the Solars to an idea of a return to a glorious civilization, then , again, we should be really be looking at the Path of Bronze and Path of Gold). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Yes, I know there are people who will look at the idea that the other Exalted are not naturals to the task of guiding and renewing the world as a suggestion that they are worthless and incompetent compared to the Solars, to whom they are obligated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't view people as worthless without such a role. Categorically. It's not about whether anyone is worthless without a particular quality, more about what the most interesting to realise them is, and one that captures the breadth of human character and potential.<br /> <br /> * A Nephilpal** quote this made me consider <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaranephilpal/SubjectiveMorality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789440#post789440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Subjective morality is what lets each Exalted type embody a genre of mythic hero and let those archetypes coexist and/or battle for control of the future:<br /> <br /> On the one hand, you have these divine bureaucrat-warrior monks who literally write and enforce the status quo. They want to preserve the strangehold of divine authority because it preserves their own power, but the nobler among them believe that they should maintain The System because it demonstrably works. Even the fall and overthrow of the Solars, an apocalyptic plague, a massive alien invasion and a cold war between superpowers armed with cosmic weapons hasn't been able to end the world as long as The System was intact. The Sidereals have the least mythic allusions behind them, unless you consider them angels, in which case it gets weird.<br /> <br /> So let's turn to the Dragon-Blooded, who are the lesser proponents of The System, in that they are warrior aristocrats who wish to spread their empire to the far corners of the world, bringing the glories (and horrors) of civilization to all. It's hard to view the Dynasty as terribly heroic, though, given their excesses. So I'll skip ahead.<br /> <br /> Now we get to the interesting dichotomy: Lunar vs. Solar.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, the Lunars champion a more elegant simplicity rooted in a lower population tribal model. Life is hard and harsh, but that means evolution can function again to help humanity grow stronger and more capable of surviving whatever apocalypse the enemies of the world can unleash. The Lunar tribal model eschews the trap of non-local interdependency brought by widespread commerce and replaces the deceptions of so-called civilized etiquette with tested meritocracy and straightforward taboo laws. As heroes, the Lunars are very Norse heroes, whose heroism is rooted in the delicate balance between bravery and cunning.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Solars are the Lawgivers. They build civilizations, utopias, dreams made manifest. They build shining cities and skyships and geomantic power distributors for the weather machines that let the crops grow year round. They build agriculture, commerce, tiered bureucracies enchanted for efficiency and warded against corruption. They are like Gilgamesh, Odysseus, Daedelus and Aeneas, visionary god-kings of unlimited potential. But their way creates sophistication, inequity of social classes, irrelevance of mortal meritocracy compared with Solar grandeur and the power of Solar magic to elevate the lowliest but favored to greatness over the wisest and noblest.<br /> <br /> Even setting aside the futures that the Sidereals or Terrestrials would shape, the Solar and Lunar models each have their pros and cons. But they can't both win. So, subjective morality time. Who should win, the Norse or the Greeks?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is actually doing specifically what Isator does not like (and I suspect this is what you're thinking of IL, even without directly referencing it).<br /> <br /> Now setting aside whether he was right with the specific identities of the splats (is it the right focus / breadth?) and how sympathetic they each actually are, that kind of view of a setting where each of the different types of Exalted have some measure of challenge to the ideal of heroism the other offers, seems interesting, to me.<br /> <br /> At the very least, evidently, I would guess, not at all out of step with the conversations he'd had with the developers and other writers up to that point, late First Edition IRC. So very questionable that an approach where different Exalted direct at times conflicting forms of heroism has a direct contradiction to the thesis and purpose of the game and setting, as it was imagined then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T07:41:11-08:00","id":789724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789719#post789719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, you have a choice between using Evocations and using DBT. This is on a form by form basis; you can develop both if you want, but you can only use one of them at a time. So if you want a Lunar with a really neat magic sword, you probably won't be using DBT all that often.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also not the intent of the devs that DBT be necessary for a Lunar swordsman to be competitive, Evocations or no Evocations, or that they simply come off as Exalted of Animals, judging from past q&amp;a quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T09:00:16-08:00","id":789769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, you have a choice between using Evocations and using DBT. This is on a form by form basis; you can develop both if you want, but you can only use one of them at a time. So if you want a Lunar with a really neat magic sword, you probably won't be using DBT all that often.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure Lunars will have more things to choose from than &quot;warform or Evocations (also martial arts)&quot;. I'm not sure if there will be any particular incentive to not buy or use the warform beyond the general opportunity cost of &quot;buying this cool thing means not buying or delaying buying this other cool thing that you want more&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T09:35:49-08:00","id":789786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789716#post789716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost the whole thing is dreadful hyperbole, but at least could stand as an uncharitable and biased interpretation of what has been presented, but <i>this</i>: This is a <i>fabrication</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I was just upset. I am sorry.<br /> However, I am afraid of how the Lunars are being developed. The devs and writers <i>say</i> that they are trying to avoid the problems of the past, but we don't have much true evidence of that. All we really have so far is that Lunars are angry, tattooed shape-shifters. (Add the word teenage and we've got a new TV show) That's all we had for two editions. And, yes, I would say that the connection between the moon and beasts is tenuous at best. The Lunars' concept at this point seems very weak and what I took from Mr. Vance's statement was that the creative team thinks that it is ok for Lunars to be on the same power level as Dragon-Blooded despite their fewer number.<br /> I've calmed down now and I'm sure that's not what he intended. I'm also sure they have more stuff to give us as time goes on. Again, I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> ...This is kinda my Bat Credit Card, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hi, I'm Smiles With Fangs. I backed Exalted 3rd edition, but I can't make the image I have smaller so here's a kitten<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.sherv.net/cm/emoticons/cats/kitten-lick-smiley-emoticon.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> I made some Liminal Charms <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/774800-liminal-charms-creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I made some Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> I'm working on a splat for the Moonsilver Warriors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/954420-the-moonsilver-warriors-peach\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8574-smileswithfangs","name":"SmilesWithFangs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T09:46:31-08:00","id":789794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789720#post789720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with legitimacy, I would note the books pretty much say &quot;will destroy or save&quot; the first time the Solars are mentioned. That is the deal. The Exalted don't get a guarantee that they are a necessary or righteous force in shaping the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current perspective on that is that it's a matter of the Solars not being infallible, so that being a returned hero at the end of history means you have very little latitude to screw up, and nobody is giving you a guide book of what the correct thing to do is, because there isn't one.<br /> <br /> You might have a Solar who is going all Genghis Khan across half of Creation with the perspective that the unification and the reopened trade routes and the renewed communications will be to the long term practical and spiritual benefits of the people for centuries to come (in terms of things like &quot;the increased commerce will ward off the Wyld&quot;, &quot;the better travel and communications will allow us to effectively fight off Fair Folk armies&quot; and &quot;people exchanging with and speaking to one another will have a richer experience&quot;), which makes it worth the deaths of millions. You might have another Solar who opposes that one, convinced that the devastation will actually serve as the final nail in their coffin, and that it's just plain unconscionable besides and moral compromises cannot be accepted even in the face of Armageddon. Both of them are highly qualified for their respective vocations, so let us assume that it is legitimate for either of them to be taking on such tasks. Which one is correct? Does either of them being correct mean that their position can be condoned; is it right to save the world if it requires the deaths of tens of millions? Is it right to save tens of millions of doing so will perpetuate something that will destroy the world? You'd better hope these Solars solve the dispute quickly, because being distracted against one another is giving those Fair Folk a good opportunity to come in and finish things off.<br /> <br /> I find that to be a decent enough way to preserve the idea of compelling drama and moral ambiguity amidst the return of the Solar Exalted, and a mechanism by which they may hasten the world's doom, without having to fall back on the possibility that people given tremendous power may turn out to be ungovernable monsters. Solars daunted by the tremendous size of the task ahead of them, and the possible uncertainties of how to deal with that task, without needing to fall back on the idea that they'll be uninterested or unqualified.<br /> <br /> I think one can garner sufficient drama and complexity without having to fall back on appealing to current attitudes of authority being inherently untrustworthy and corruptible.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes it clear that when I posit the Solars as legitimate and necessary, I'm not suggesting a game in which they're always right, or even always nice people. Just that, barring the corruption of the Great Curse, they'll be people who are trying to pursue things that, one way or another, further the well-being of people and/or the world in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not the TSR is the right way to approach it (and there are problems with it, as it stands, primarily I think of anachronism and the underlying cultural logic behind it), in many ways it is not challenging the Solar narrative and theme in a way that is not already present through the Bronze Faction (which in that instance is probably to their advantage as making an interesting splat) and writing within the 1e and 2e cores about who and what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the tension of the Bronze Faction is that we can't fully take their assessment of the situation at face value, because there are gaps in their knowledge.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe that's the case with the Thousand Streams River as well, but I think there's an issue in how it appeals very directly to certain biases, such that it quickly gets held up as the highest moral standard of the setting, without much consideration for how this might be counterproductive. I wouldn't say I don't think <i>anybody</i> has ever held up the Bronze Faction as righteously standing against the inherent tyranny of all figures of power, but their own fallacies appear on display enough to make it a good deal less prominent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With whether the TSR implies that the Solars must shape the world a particular way, I don't think it ever did. At the most it implied there were tendencies there in the nature of their power and how they express it that skewed them towards a particular and in ways particularly unstable form of society, while the Lunars returned, with a specific cultural experience the Solars lacked were able to look at things differently not a mandated destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still find that to be too far. There's just... there's really no reason why you couldn't have a Solar whose model for saving the world and renewing good conduct among humanity is based on engineering and safeguarding a kind of agrarian or foraging primitivist society, and once that's in there it's hard to let go of the point that they'd be extremely good at it, and probably better at it than a Lunar (not least because I'm having difficulty seeing Lunars as naturally having Charms to manage people and navigate interactions in a manner that's good for social engineering in general, let alone towards a particular kind of society).<br /> <br /> Still, if it's the point that the <u>perspective</u> that different Exalted might create different societies for reasons apart from their Charms being limited to such is credible, then I'll agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't view people as worthless without such a role.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, hey, you don't need to be overturning the paradigm to be accomplished and powerful within the paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Categorically. It's not about whether anyone is worthless without a particular quality, more about what the most interesting to realise them is, and one that captures the breadth of human character and potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my thought that Lunars, having been freed from the shackles of the conflicted Second Age, become individuals mighty enough to do as they please without being confined (while also not becoming some kind of exemplars of anarchism; a Lunar does not need to care about the existence of authorities to hold themselves as being powerful enough to not be subject to them) can accomplish that nicely.<br /> <br /> (On that note: I swear, I'm not trying to turn this Lunar thread into a Solar one, it's just that I'm struck by the idea that knowing what Lunars are is enabled by knowing what Solars are)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A Nephilpal** quote this made me consider<br /> <br /> Now this is actually doing specifically what Isator does not like (and I suspect this is what you're thinking of IL, even without directly referencing it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the points he actually makes, I think he's misapplying the term &quot;subjective morality&quot;, nor do I think such a consideration is necessary to make the dispute he presents credible and interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now setting aside whether he was right with the specific identities of the splats (is it the right focus / breadth?) and how sympathetic they each actually are, that kind of view of a setting where each of the different types of Exalted have some measure of challenge to the ideal of heroism the other offers, seems interesting, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the good points of it can be applied to the matter of their context rather than their qualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, evidently, I would guess, not at all out of step with the conversations he'd had with the developers and other writers up to that point, late First Edition IRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would not be my guess; it's my view that Nephilpal was often going off on his own tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So very questionable that an approach where different Exalted direct at times conflicting forms of heroism has a direct contradiction to the thesis and purpose of the game and setting, as it was imagined then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could find the quote from one of Grabowski's outlines in question, and let you judge for yourself?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T10:02:38-08:00","id":789801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All we really have so far is that Lunars are angry, tattooed shape-shifters. (Add the word teenage and we've got a new TV show) That's all we had for two editions.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a point where I'm going to start feeling impeded by contextually ambiguous syntax, because I'm uncertain whether or not to read this sentence as &quot;we (the fans)&quot; or &quot;we (the Lunars themselves)&quot;. That being said, no, that is not all the corebook portrays, and yes, the corebook provides details and texture distinct from the prior Editions. (For that matter, it's not even the sole features the Lunars had in prior Editions) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that the connection between the moon and beasts is tenuous at best.</div> </div> </div> </div> It has featured through numerous mythologies, mysticisms and folklore for extended periods of history; the Moon as exemplary of the night, the night as something quintessentially outside the domain of man, a time for the untamed. You're seeing &quot;Chosen of Animals&quot;, I am seeing &quot;Chosen of something that subordinates animals within itself&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what I took from Mr. Vance's statement was that the creative team thinks that it is ok for Lunars to be on the same power level as Dragon-Blooded despite their fewer number.</div> </div> </div> </div> That... wha... no. Saying &quot;nailing down the terms Celestial and Terrestrial is meaningless&quot; does not mean &quot;it doesn't even matter if Lunars are Celestial, we're gonna make 'em weak anyway&quot;, it means &quot;it doesn't really matter if you can semantically prove whether or not animals are a Terrestrial association, because we're not treating those categories as hard things we need to adhere to like that&quot;. Terrestrial means little to nothing, so rigarously proving that animals be associated with it neither means that Lunars are Terrestrial, nor that they not be among the most powerful Exalted. The Exalted will be decided on their merits, not on adhering to useless categories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T10:09:24-08:00","id":789805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789786#post789786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...what I took from Mr. Vance's statement was that the creative team thinks that it is ok for Lunars to be on the same power level as Dragon-Blooded despite their fewer number.</div> </div> </div> </div>...wut? I'm not sure how you could do that. Especially since he is not the person who would even decide that, had that even been inferred in his statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T10:33:28-08:00","id":789815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789786#post789786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars' concept at this point seems very weak and what I took from Mr. Vance's statement was that the creative team thinks that it is ok for Lunars to be on the same power level as Dragon-Blooded despite their fewer number.<br /> ...This is kinda my Bat Credit Card, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme try and get at what I was really saying. If I were to say that Odysseus was Celestial, and that Wong Fei Hung was Terrestrial, that statement conveys zero information outside the context of Exalted. But when I say that Odysseus is cunning and that Wong Fei Hung is a master of martial arts, that tells you something about their character. Trying to classify the themes of a type of Exalted into that dichotomy isn't going to be very helpful\u2014if animals are a terrestrial purview, then certainly humans are too, and the most powerful of Exalted evoke incredible prowess of human skill, so that can't be right.<br /> <br /> Are Lunars on the same power level as Terrestrials? Haha, jesus, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T16:16:36-08:00","id":789971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789720#post789720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A Nephilpal** quote this made me consider<br /> <br /> Now this is actually doing specifically what Isator does not like (and I suspect this is what you're thinking of IL, even without directly referencing it).<br /> <br /> Now setting aside whether he was right with the specific identities of the splats (is it the right focus / breadth?) and how sympathetic they each actually are, that kind of view of a setting where each of the different types of Exalted have some measure of challenge to the ideal of heroism the other offers, seems interesting, to me.<br /> <br /> At the very least, evidently, I would guess, not at all out of step with the conversations he'd had with the developers and other writers up to that point, late First Edition IRC. So very questionable that an approach where different Exalted direct at times conflicting forms of heroism has a direct contradiction to the thesis and purpose of the game and setting, as it was imagined then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Wow. Had Nephilpal just finished Deus Ex and taken the Tracer Tong ending? Because that is...<i>incredibly </i>mawkish and dumb for anyone not caught in the grip of late nineties &quot;yeah man fight the system smash the machine free your miiiiiind&quot; total misunderstanding of dialectical materialism. Also hilarious is the supposition of some fundamental conflict between Classical Greek and Epic Norse worldviews, and that either of them was ideologically anti-civilization.<br /> <br /> Lunars should not be anti-civilization because of some gross Social Darwinism worldview that doesn't even make sense for the Chosen of Lamarck-by-way-of-Kirby. They should not be anti-civilization in general. They should be against <i>specific </i>civilizations because those civilizations are trying to <i>murder them </i>and to destroy, pillage, or subjugate their <i>own </i>civilizations. They don't tear down satrapies stone by stone because INDOOR PLUMBING MAKES YOU WEAK, they do it because those satrapies host soldiers of the Realm who brutalize them and theirs, and granaries and stockpiles that feed and arm those soldiers, enabling campaigns of conquest and subjugation.<br /> <br /> The Dev Diary on Perfect Soul did a lot to allay my concerns about both Solars and Lunars in Third Edition, because it did away with the long-running and insidious idea that Solars are immune to moral conflict, except when their Magic Asshole Timer runs out, and that Lunars would be shunted into the roles of designated villainy because man, <i>their</i> revolution is just so, like, <i>uncivilized.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T16:54:35-08:00","id":789983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789971#post789971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Wow. Had Nephilpal just finished Deus Ex and taken the Tracer Tong ending? Because that is...<i>incredibly </i>mawkish and dumb for anyone not caught in the grip of late nineties &quot;yeah man fight the system smash the machine free your miiiiiind&quot; total misunderstanding of dialectical materialism. Also hilarious is the supposition of some fundamental conflict between Classical Greek and Epic Norse worldviews, and that either of them was ideologically anti-civilization.<br /> <br /> Lunars should not be anti-civilization because of some gross Social Darwinism worldview that doesn't even make sense for the Chosen of Lamarck-by-way-of-Kirby. They should not be anti-civilization in general. They should be against <i>specific </i>civilizations because those civilizations are trying to <i>murder them </i>and to destroy, pillage, or subjugate their <i>own </i>civilizations. They don't tear down satrapies stone by stone because INDOOR PLUMBING MAKES YOU WEAK, they do it because those satrapies host soldiers of the Realm who brutalize them and theirs, and granaries and stockpiles that feed and arm those soldiers, enabling campaigns of conquest and subjugation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was likewise remembering Holden's essay on the differences between Aesthetic Barbarism, Practical Barbarism, and Ideological Barbarism.<br /> <br /> Neph's idea seems to fit squarely within the fallacy of Ideological Barbarism, which is something I'm looking forward to Lunar material finally moving away from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dev Diary on Perfect Soul did a lot to allay my concerns about both Solars and Lunars in Third Edition, because it did away with the long-running and insidious idea that Solars are immune to moral conflict, except when their Magic Asshole Timer runs out, and that Lunars would be shunted into the roles of designated villainy because man, <i>their</i> revolution is just so, like, <i>uncivilized.</i> </div> </div> </div>I might have to read that, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T18:38:18-08:00","id":790022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmilesWithFangs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789786#post789786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. I was just upset. I am sorry.<br /> However, I am afraid of how the Lunars are being developed. The devs and writers <i>say</i> that they are trying to avoid the problems of the past, but we don't have much true evidence of that. All we really have so far is that Lunars are angry, tattooed shape-shifters. (Add the word teenage and we've got a new TV show) That's all we had for two editions. And, yes, I would say that the connection between the moon and beasts is tenuous at best. The Lunars' concept at this point seems very weak and what I took from Mr. Vance's statement was that the creative team thinks that it is ok for Lunars to be on the same power level as Dragon-Blooded despite their fewer number.<br /> I've calmed down now and I'm sure that's not what he intended. I'm also sure they have more stuff to give us as time goes on. Again, I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> ...This is kinda my Bat Credit Card, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, there seems to be a widespread &quot;see what you will&quot; factor with Lunars. You see shapeshifting into beasts, hulking out, touching on a collective unconscious and various other factors as inherently weak. I'm guessing that it might have something to do with the media being consumed, as in at least one case on the GitP forums it seemed to be related to someone highly lowballing the concept of &quot;werewolf&quot;, on account of the fact that there aren't any actual werewolves around to compare, not that realism arguments actually factor in here.<br /> <br /> But the only reason that someone would do that is because they're familiar with more media that lowball werewolves or restrict their capabilities than ones that place them noticeably higher up and expand upon what they are. If your only reference point is The Wolfman, Werewolf: the Apocalypse might come as a terrible shock. Likewise, Lunars, which are both even more powerful and yet based on a similar concept; if you're still on Lon Chaney, your expectations will remain incredibly low..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:56:13-08:00","id":790438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789971#post789971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Wow. Had Nephilpal just finished Deus Ex and taken the Tracer Tong ending? Because that is...<i>incredibly </i>mawkish and dumb for anyone not caught in the grip of late nineties &quot;yeah man fight the system smash the machine free your miiiiiind&quot; total misunderstanding of dialectical materialism. Also hilarious is the supposition of some fundamental conflict between Classical Greek and Epic Norse worldviews, and that either of them was ideologically anti-civilization.[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty harsh.<br /> There really probably was a clash between Classical Greek and Norse worldviews, to be honest (to the extent we can talk about a single cultural worldview). They *were* different cultures and classical Greece was a pretty different place to Scandinavia between the fall of Rome and before Christianisation and the Medieval period. The Greek heroes themselves are pre-classical, so in a sense don't fully embody the differences between these two cultures though (and whether Solars and Lunars really do or don't). And of course I agree that the Norse weren't really anachronistically ideologically anti-civilization though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=789971#post789971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should be against <i>specific </i>civilizations because those civilizations are trying to <i>murder them </i>and to destroy, pillage, or subjugate their <i>own </i>civilizations. They don't tear down satrapies stone by stone because INDOOR PLUMBING MAKES YOU WEAK, they do it because those satrapies host soldiers of the Realm who brutalize them and theirs, and granaries and stockpiles that feed and arm those soldiers, enabling campaigns of conquest and subjugation.[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thesaurasaurus, this'll probably be tl;dr and only partly a response to your comment (and part some thoughts that spun off from it) -<br /> <br /> To be fair, in 1e and also 2e as written that would have made close to zero sense. IRC the Lunars were voluntary exiles of the Old Realm, were either the masters who controlled or were free wanderers of large swathes of Creation where the Realm had never had much control (not a constantly shifting mosaic of battlefields), and which were where Lunars normally came to exaltation and lived. Subject to the Wyld Hunt, yes, but when they strayed into the territory of the Dragonblooded. Maybe their elders, only, even knew what a Sidereal was.<br /> <br /> The task before the writers was explaining *why* the Lunars abandoned the Solars' First Age civilization for the Wyld, to not even try and sustain it in any form. Because they were *not* driven out.<br /> <br /> That's where those two ideological frameworks (the Silver Pact and Thousand Streams River) came from.<br /> <br /> The idea seems like that, kind of like the Bronze Faction although on opposed grounds, they were pursuing a vision of a Creation that would not be vulnerable to the same collapse and danger of the First Age. (Arguably this made the Silver Pact and Thousand Streams River like a second worse Bronze Faction, and some of the points in Isator's post constrasting these seem to explain why pretty well).<br /> <br /> That's why we got Lunars who were pursuing a legacy of ideological violence against the inheritors of the civilization of the First Age, though. Attacks that had stepped up with the Empress gone, and where the Lunars were at least as much the originators of violence of suspect justification against the Realm, as the other way around. <br /> Let's understand the ideas of the Lunars which were presented in their own context. (As much as is that what we want? It seems not.)<br /> <br /> The present day writers have said, as far as I can tell, &quot;Hmm. Well, that stuff didn't work. So let's take a simpler and more direct route. Why not just have them be driven out of the Realm and be making ceaseless war against it for that reason?&quot; and that's why we're getting what we get. The Lunars were driven off. They're pissed! (and just letting go and acting is peacemakers is much harder because of a magical hole in their soul). No ideology this time. Just pragmatism, revenge and the desire for power. These Lunars seem like they'll be sold on the idea that being an angry, crafty, ruthless beast with a legitimate beef and a human heart inside can be really, really wicked fun. You are gonna be shapechanging berserkers that berserk, and shapechanging tricksters who trick, and shapechanging shamans* who er... shaman, and you'll love it, because we'll do it really well.<br /> <br /> Now I think some of the fans of the game, and of the Lunars, are going to see this and go, more or less - &quot;We had Lunars who, in theory, engaged with the kind of questions that were raised by characters like Perfect Soul (see Perfect Soul thread). Of leaders making choices about societies. They did so, it seemed, from a distinctly different angle and social context to than the Solars. I can practice intrigue and violence in most any game and those were distinctively Exalted questions and ideas and a distinctively Exalted genre. Those were a unique kind of shapeshifting hero. Now we have Lunars who don't seem to engage with those same questions. They're not seemly engaging with building and nurturing societies and peoples as anything other than temporary, expedient tools for destruction and revenge. So how is this better? Is this worthy of Exalted?&quot;. Trying not to put words in anyone's mouth, this is just as I imagine in my mind's eye some unknown number of people (could be almost none, could be a few) responding.<br /> <br /> Obviously to some degree, some of the counter here is &quot;Well, they're beast shapeshifters of the least apparently moral and most apparently chaotic of the gods. Why should they even engage with those questions at all, at a scale beyond engaging with and acting as foils and allies to Solars who actually do? The TSR and Silver Pact made no real sense. Setting Lunars to even engage questions of how societies should work with the power to practically shape that undermines Solar games where they are expected to, and undermines the Lunars as the Lunars must by necessity be much weaker here than the Solars, which looks bad and makes them merely weaker Solars of limited achievement that no one would want to play.&quot;. And I think there's about as good an argument made for that perspective here as can be made, and I can't really say it is wrong (as much as I find it slightly unsatisfying).<br /> <br /> (By the way, Isator, just for info in case you did want to know, just to say I did read through your post, and appreciated the response. More interesting thought provoking than anything I had any specific comments for or against.)<br /> <br /> *Kind of a side thought on &quot;shapechanging shamans&quot; is of whether &quot;By becoming the beast, you have mystic sympathy in tune with the occult and spirit world and thereby gain magical powers, visions and insights&quot; is fertile ground for any Lunars Charms - shapechanging as a ritual spell component of a sort of its own that only Lunars can access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:33:34-08:00","id":790454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790438#post790438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I think some of the fans of the game, and of the Lunars, are going to see this and go, more or less - &quot;We had Lunars who, in theory, engaged with the kind of questions that were raised by characters like Perfect Soul (see Perfect Soul thread). Of leaders making choices about societies. They did so, it seemed, from a distinctly different angle and social context to than the Solars. I can practice intrigue and violence in most any game and those were distinctively Exalted questions and ideas and a distinctively Exalted genre. Those were a unique kind of shapeshifting hero. Now we have Lunars who don't seem to engage with those same questions. They're not seemly engaging with building and nurturing societies and peoples as anything other than temporary, expedient tools for destruction and revenge. So how is this better? Is this worthy of Exalted?&quot;. Trying not to put words in anyone's mouth, this is just as I imagine in my mind's eye some unknown number of people (could be almost none, could be a few) responding.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can add at least +1 to the count of people experiencing that response. You've very coherently summed up my own feelings and the origin of my dissatisfaction with what we know, so far, of 3E's Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T14:24:42-08:00","id":790487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I think some of the fans of the game, and of the Lunars, are going to see this and go, more or less - &quot;We had Lunars who, in theory, engaged with the kind of questions that were raised by characters like Perfect Soul (see Perfect Soul thread). Of leaders making choices about societies. They did so, it seemed, from a distinctly different angle and social context to than the Solars. I can practice intrigue and violence in most any game and those were distinctively Exalted questions and ideas and a distinctively Exalted genre. Those were a unique kind of shapeshifting hero. Now we have Lunars who don't seem to engage with those same questions. They're not seemly engaging with building and nurturing societies and peoples as anything other than temporary, expedient tools for destruction and revenge. So how is this better? Is this worthy of Exalted?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> My first thought in response to this: the corebook makes two references that I can recall (in the section dedicated to the Lunars, and for Ma-Ha-Suchi) that the return of the Solars is provoking or concordant with some ambiguous feelings. I think part of that could be the idea of some struggling against the moral and essential drive for participation in the world and taking up a role in the new Age; of a Lunar who is trying to decide what they would actually do in a world where nothing else is constraining them, including whether they want to enter into what could be considered a new form of constraint (and if it's not what one wants, whether they should do it anyway). I've said that the motivation to have a world in which they can do as they please might be a big part of what they think they want, but I by no means think it's something they should be untroubled about getting. I see a lot of potential in John's statement of them as people who are trying to find who they are; I think the search for identity, and how it expresses the use of power, can be sophisticated as anything else, and worthy of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T14:29:40-08:00","id":790491,"title":"","content":"You should never underestimate the power of violence applied thoughtfully, prudently, competently, and unromantically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T18:01:11-08:00","id":790593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790438#post790438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty harsh.<br /> There really probably was a clash between Classical Greek and Norse worldviews, to be honest (to the extent we can talk about a single cultural worldview). They *were* different cultures and classical Greece was a pretty different place to Scandinavia between the fall of Rome and before Christianisation and the Medieval period. The Greek heroes themselves are pre-classical, so in a sense don't fully embody the differences between these two cultures though (and whether Solars and Lunars really do or don't). And of course I agree that the Norse weren't really anachronistically ideologically anti-civilization though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were both civilizations who sustained themselves on a mixture of herding and sedentary agriculture, then later added in periodic raiding against their neighbors when subsistence farming wasn't enough to keep pace with their growth, driven by advances in metallurgy, architecture, and shipbuilding and facilitated by bordering coastlines. Both based their military dominance on a combination of naval superiority and sophisticated infantry formation tactics, and later progressed to leaving local authorities in power in exchange for regular tribute in lieu of sacking and plundering them.<br /> <br /> They both believed in pantheons of worldly deities with fundamentally-human motives but vast and transcendental power, headed by celestial Allfather figures who had (singly or collectively) overthrown their progenitors and fashioned the world from their corpses. These deities were fickle and capricious, holding moral authority by virtue of aggressively fucking up anyone who challenged them, but were themselves bound by a greater pattern woven by a trio of capital-F Fates who were even more remote and unknowable than the gods. Each god prized certain virtues in mortals, but their favor could also be bought with the right brand of sacrifice, which increasingly meant castes of priests acting as mercenary intercessionaries who jealously guarded their prayers and rituals until the temporal authorities got sick of it and curtailed their power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790438#post790438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thesaurasaurus, this'll probably be tl;dr and only partly a response to your comment (and part some thoughts that spun off from it) -<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> That's why we got Lunars who were pursuing a legacy of ideological violence against the inheritors of the civilization of the First Age, though. Attacks that had stepped up with the Empress gone, and where the Lunars were at least as much the originators of violence of suspect justification against the Realm, as the other way around.<br /> Let's understand the ideas of the Lunars which were presented in their own context. (As much as is that what we want? It seems not.)<br /> <br /> The present day writers have said, as far as I can tell, &quot;Hmm. Well, that stuff didn't work. So let's take a simpler and more direct route. Why not just have them be driven out of the Realm and be making ceaseless war against it for that reason?&quot; and that's why we're getting what we get. The Lunars were driven off. They're pissed! (and just letting go and acting is peacemakers is much harder because of a magical hole in their soul). No ideology this time. Just pragmatism, revenge and the desire for power. These Lunars seem like they'll be sold on the idea that being an angry, crafty, ruthless beast with a legitimate beef and a human heart inside can be really, really wicked fun. You are gonna be shapechanging berserkers that berserk, and shapechanging tricksters who trick, and shapechanging shamans* who er... shaman, and you'll love it, because we'll do it really well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This portrayal grates on me for several reasons, but the strongest one, and the one I can most clearly articulate, is that violence against and exploitation of the periphery for the benefit of the center is <i>what empire is</i>. A peaceful, or at least comparatively-benign empire is an oxymoron. There is no forgive-and-forget - your option are 'kneel', 'fight back', or 'die' (the latter of which does not preclude the former two). An empire that can no longer expand is an empire that's about to implode. If there's peace (and not make-a-desert-and-call-it-peace), it's because you've cost them enough blood and treasure that they decided to cut their losses.<br /> <br /> With all of this, a magical hole in Lunars' souls seems redundant and unnecessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790438#post790438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I think some of the fans of the game, and of the Lunars, are going to see this and go, more or less - &quot;We had Lunars who, in theory, engaged with the kind of questions that were raised by characters like Perfect Soul (see Perfect Soul thread). Of leaders making choices about societies. They did so, it seemed, from a distinctly different angle and social context to than the Solars. I can practice intrigue and violence in most any game and those were distinctively Exalted questions and ideas and a distinctively Exalted genre. Those were a unique kind of shapeshifting hero. Now we have Lunars who don't seem to engage with those same questions. They're not seemly engaging with building and nurturing societies and peoples as anything other than temporary, expedient tools for destruction and revenge. So how is this better? Is this worthy of Exalted?&quot;. Trying not to put words in anyone's mouth, this is just as I imagine in my mind's eye some unknown number of people (could be almost none, could be a few) responding.<br /> <br /> Obviously to some degree, some of the counter here is &quot;Well, they're beast shapeshifters of the least apparently moral and most apparently chaotic of the gods. Why should they even engage with those questions at all, at a scale beyond engaging with and acting as foils and allies to Solars who actually do? The TSR and Silver Pact made no real sense. Setting Lunars to even engage questions of how societies should work with the power to practically shape that undermines Solar games where they are expected to, and undermines the Lunars as the Lunars must by necessity be much weaker here than the Solars, which looks bad and makes them merely weaker Solars of limited achievement that no one would want to play.&quot;. And I think there's about as good an argument made for that perspective here as can be made, and I can't really say it is wrong (as much as I find it slightly unsatisfying).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really don't want Lunars to become ISIS. There is <i>nothing </i>sympathetic nor admirable about ISIS.<br /> <br /> Also, if &quot;Solars already do that&quot; was grounds for locking other splats out of stories, nobody but Solars would ever get to do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:54:43-08:00","id":790958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790438#post790438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IRC the Lunars were voluntary exiles of the Old Realm</div> </div> </div> </div>This was never true. They were always violently displaced refugees who were driven beyond the boundaries of the world, into the Wyld where the Dragon-Blooded could not follow, and who only really had any safety returning to Creation after the Great Contagion caused the collapse of the Creation-spanning Shogunate. At the very soonest, no significant number of Lunars dared to return to Creation until after the Shogunate had begun to fracture with its many civil wars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The task before the writers was explaining *why* the Lunars abandoned the Solars' First Age civilization for the Wyld, to not even try and sustain it in any form. Because they were *not* driven out.<br /> <br /> That's where those two ideological frameworks (the Silver Pact and Thousand Streams River) came from. </div> </div> </div>Then they were useless from conception.<br /> <br /> Both because the Lunars had been driven out, <i>and </i>because sustaining it in any form would be impossible so long as the vast majority of Solar Exalted were missing, the few Solar Exalted remaining became lightning rods for the full, unified might of the Shogunate and their Sidereal backers, and the Sidereals and Shogunate made a secondary priority of chasing a Lunar away from any First Age kingdom or wonder that the Lunar managed to build or salvage, at which point the Lunar would find that wonder being used to hunt her to death.<br /> <br /> Even today, Lunars can only what the Scarlet Empire doesn't really care to TAKE. The Caul remains contested in the modern day only because most of the Empire has already written the place off as a loss; if the entire Dynasty decided as one to drive the Anathema away and take back their heritage, the Lunar Exalted would have no choice but to flee or die.<br /> <br /> And that's with a significant percentage of the 400 Lunar Exalted working together to hold the place. There were much, much fewer Lunars guarding private kingdoms built around First Age manses after the rise of the Shogunate; easily overwhelmed by the might of a Gens / Legion or two, especially with the Sidereals helping.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea seems like that, kind of like the Bronze Faction although on opposed grounds, they were pursuing a vision of a Creation that would not be vulnerable to the same collapse and danger of the First Age. </div> </div> </div>Except &quot;not dying&quot; should have been a higher priority, so Lunars would make sure to stay mobile and never build anything that they couldn't freely abandon if the Dragon-Blooded came marching in. And if the Lunar built something valuable enough that she wouldn't want to abandon it, it would surely be valuable enough that the Dragon-Blooded would come marching in to take it or destroy it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> be making ceaseless war against it for that reason?&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Putting an end to the Empire that won't ever stop trying to kill them&quot; sounds like a reason to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I think some of the fans of the game, and of the Lunars, are going to see this and go, more or less - &quot;We had Lunars who, in theory, engaged with the kind of questions that were raised by characters like Perfect Soul (see Perfect Soul thread). Of leaders making choices about societies. They did so, it seemed, from a distinctly different angle and social context to than the Solars. I can practice intrigue and violence in most any game and those were distinctively Exalted questions and ideas and a distinctively Exalted genre. Those were a unique kind of shapeshifting hero. Now we have Lunars who don't seem to engage with those same questions. </div> </div> </div>Why would Lunars need to engage with those questions when the Solar Exalted are better suited for doing so?<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted are in a place very similar to the Lunar Exalted right now, but with less baggage against the Scarlet Empire and with MORE power to guide and shape societies according to their visions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously to some degree, some of the counter here is &quot;Well, they're beast shapeshifters of the least apparently moral and most apparently chaotic of the gods. Why should they even engage with those questions at all, at a scale beyond engaging with and acting as foils and allies to Solars who actually do? The TSR and Silver Pact made no real sense. Setting Lunars to even engage questions of how societies should work with the power to practically shape that undermines Solar games where they are expected to, and undermines the Lunars as the Lunars must by necessity be much weaker here than the Solars, which looks bad and makes them merely weaker Solars of limited achievement that no one would want to play.&quot;. And I think there's about as good an argument made for that perspective here as can be made, and I can't really say it is wrong (as much as I find it slightly unsatisfying). </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, there are still the Solar Exalted for playing as the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Thousand Streams River was Second Edition trying to make Lunars more like Solars, and it just doesn't work. Their places and potentials within the setting are too different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:21:28-08:00","id":790988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790593#post790593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were both civilizations who sustained themselves on a mixture of herding and sedentary agriculture, then later added in periodic raiding against their neighbors when subsistence farming wasn't enough to keep pace with their growth, driven by advances in metallurgy, architecture, and shipbuilding and facilitated by bordering coastlines. Both based their military dominance on a combination of naval superiority and sophisticated infantry formation tactics, and later progressed to leaving local authorities in power in exchange for regular tribute in lieu of sacking and plundering them.<br /> <br /> They both believed in pantheons of worldly deities with fundamentally-human motives but vast and transcendental power, headed by celestial Allfather figures who had (singly or collectively) overthrown their progenitors and fashioned the world from their corpses. These deities were fickle and capricious, holding moral authority by virtue of aggressively fucking up anyone who challenged them, but were themselves bound by a greater pattern woven by a trio of capital-F Fates who were even more remote and unknowable than the gods. Each god prized certain virtues in mortals, but their favor could also be bought with the right brand of sacrifice, which increasingly meant castes of priests acting as mercenary intercessionaries who jealously guarded their prayers and rituals until the temporal authorities got sick of it and curtailed their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they were both descendants of Proto-Indo European religion, yes. And I suppose the other similarities stand, although I wasn't totally aware the Classical Greeks went a-viking though. <br /> <br /> There are of course differences. <br /> <br /> For one, at the same time, one was a culture of city states, in which, at least for the Ionian Greeks, commerce with developed cultures of the Near East was frequent, and in which rich traditions of oratory gave rise to another rich tradition of philosophy.<br /> <br /> The other did not particularly have cities.<br /> <br /> I seriously do not think that many experts on Classical Greece would find tenable the idea that they did not have a quite different worldview than the Norse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790593#post790593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This portrayal grates on me for several reasons, but the strongest one, and the one I can most clearly articulate, is that violence against and exploitation of the periphery for the benefit of the center is <i>what empire is</i>. A peaceful, or at least comparatively-benign empire is an oxymoron. There is no forgive-and-forget - your option are 'kneel', 'fight back', or 'die' (the latter of which does not preclude the former two). An empire that can no longer expand is an empire that's about to implode. If there's peace (and not make-a-desert-and-call-it-peace), it's because you've cost them enough blood and treasure that they decided to cut their losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we can look at the historiography of what relations were like for societies on the borders of empires like the Ottoman, Chinese and Russian to find out to what extent that logic about &quot;kneel&quot;, &quot;fight back&quot;, or &quot;die&quot; actually applies, and also about the stability of borders over time vs decline of empires (are empires really always in decline through long periods of virtual stability of borders?). I don't know personally. Theories about why, when and where empires exist and expand (imperiogenesis) are beyond the scope of what it's worth going on a derail about here (and there are other threads on it anyways). I def. agree that, on the whole, empires don't have any internal binding nation state logic like &quot;The state is only legitimate if it governs over our nation&quot;, so powerful imperial states are going to over time tend to accrue any bordering territories which are economically worth conquering for imperial elites (the carrot), and which seem to pose potential military threat (the stick). That's particularly the case if they encounter peoples at the border who have no concept of unified government or diplomacy (diplomacy can't beat out war if you're making worthless treaties with people who either don't really hold the concept as important or don't hold any real power). (And.... I'm half going on the tangent I thought was pretty useless... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> Although it seems to me that you're getting from my statement about First Edition - &quot;The Realm does not extend or expand to certain parts of Creation, where the Lunars rule or live, from where they arise to assault the Realm in its decline&quot; - a sort of benign intention. That's something that edition, IRC, explained more in terms of those regions being relatively valueless to expend the resources and costs of occupation and expansion (which increase with distance from the centre - longer supply chains, more difficulty finding and paying competent administrators who will travel there, etc.) and a low priority generally, not anything particularly benign.<br /> <br /> (We all accept there are regions which empires do not want because it's more expensive and troublesome to govern them than their powerful people could derive any benefit from them. Although much of the time that often doesn't mean they don't take them anyway, for reasons of miscalculation or because imperial expansion is not really driven by material calculation, c.f. Scramble for Africa, in which the European powers scrambled for a bunch of what seems from consensus like more or less economically worthless territories).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790958#post790958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was never true. They were always violently displaced refugees who were driven beyond the boundaries of the world, into the Wyld where the Dragon-Blooded could not follow, and who only really had any safety returning to Creation after the Great Contagion caused the collapse of the Creation-spanning Shogunate. At the very soonest, no significant number of Lunars dared to return to Creation until after the Shogunate had begun to fracture with its many civil wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Let's read!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 1e: Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Old Realm fell the Lunar Exalted forswore the defense of the Realm and became its enemies, fleeing into the depths of the Wyld, where they could walk and others could not. Here the ancient enemies of the Realm kept the Dragon-blooded at bay, and their vast powers over beasts and illusion were strengthened by an array of dangerous animals and the shifting and malleable nature of these regions. Alas many succumbed to the maddening influences of the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 1e: The Lunars page 10, opening paragraph of the introduction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It has been a long time since the Usurpation, 15 long centuries since the Lunar Exalted <b>turned their backs on their mates</b> and fled into the wilderness on the edges of Creation. At first, their exile <b>was a willing one</b>, but as the years have passed, the Lunar Exalted have grown more and more bitter about their consignment to the wilderness. Many of the elder Lunars have come to believe that they were manipulated by the Sidereals in some fashion and many others have grown to the maturity of their power in the lands beyond the reach of civilization. These latter-day Exalts <b>never knew the First Age, or the horrors that led the Lunars to turn their backs on it</b>. They do not see themselves as exiles from civilization, but as enemies from it&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More of a mixed picture than I thought. The full articulation of Lunars in their book was exactly as I described it, while the Corebook version is sort of like the 3e version (3e has less cray-cray).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/782270-what-is-a-lunar?p=790958#post790958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Lunars need to engage with those questions when the Solar Exalted are better suited for doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably some people wish to play the chosen of a god who is Luna and characters who have the power of their form and wish to do so. I'm not saying they *need* to do anything in particular though, personally. (I suppose if they are that driven in the new edition, they may brew up some Exigents I guess).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}